            0 => 'Poison Ivy earned its following because it is light in the hand, stays round, and works with almost any hitch or device a climber is likely to own. Poison Moon uses that same 11.7 mm, 24-strand design, so the handling is what Poison Ivy users already know. The change is the color, which helps when a crew runs several climbing lines and wants each one easy to identify.',
