    '/blowers-and-other-equipment/husqvarna-525lk-combination-tool-string-trimmer/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/blowers-and-other-equipment/husqvarna-525lk-combination-tool-string-trimmer/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/blowers-and-other-equipment/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna 525LK Combination Trimmer',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'power-tool',
      'price' => 419,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna 525',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna 525LK Combi Trimmer: Husqvarna 525 Guide',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna 525LK Combi String Trimmer (Husqvarna 525 Series)',
      'meta' => 'The Husqvarna 525LK is the split-shaft version of the Husqvarna 525 trimmer: 25.4 cc, light, and ready for combi attachments. Specs, uses, and price.',
      'tagline' => 'Light 25.4 cc combi power head with a trimmer attachment.',
      'summary' => 'The Husqvarna 525LK is the split-shaft combi version of the Husqvarna 525 trimmer, pairing a light 25.4 cc engine with a coupling that accepts other combi attachments. Crews get a commercial string trimmer that can also run an edger, hedge trimmer, or pole saw.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => '25.4 cc X-Torq 2-stroke engine',
        1 => 'Split shaft accepts Husqvarna combi attachments',
        2 => 'Light, balanced power head for all-day use',
        3 => 'Loop handle for control',
        4 => 'Breaks down for compact transport',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Displacement',
          1 => '25.4 cc',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Engine',
          1 => 'X-Torq 2-stroke',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Shaft',
          1 => 'Split (combi)',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Handle',
          1 => 'Loop handle',
        ),
        4 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fuel',
          1 => 'Gas and 2-stroke oil mix',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'The Husqvarna 525 family',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Husqvarna\'s 525 series covers a group of light commercial trimmers built around the same 25.4 cc engine. The 525L has a fixed straight shaft, and the 525LK adds a split shaft so the lower half can be swapped for other attachments. If you are looking for a Husqvarna 525 weed eater that can do more than trim, the LK is the one to look at.',
            1 => 'The engine is light enough to carry for long stretches without wearing you out, yet strong enough for heavy grass and weeds around a job site.',
            2 => 'The combi coupling is quick to use. Loosen the knob, press the release, and slide the attachment out; slide the next one in until it locks, then tighten. There are no tools needed, so switching from trimming to edging takes less than a minute on site.',
            3 => 'Searches for Husqvarna 525 and 525 Husqvarna usually land on one of these two models, so it pays to check which shaft you are getting before you order.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Attachments that earn their keep',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'For tree crews, the pole saw attachment is the obvious add-on: it lets a ground worker clear low limbs, raise canopies over sidewalks, and cut small storm damage without pulling out a separate pole saw engine. An edger attachment cleans up hardscape after stump grinding, and a hedge trimmer attachment handles shrub work that often comes up on residential jobs.',
            1 => 'Each attachment snaps onto the same coupling, so you carry one engine and several lightweight shafts. Check that each attachment is listed as compatible with the 525LK coupling before buying.',
            2 => 'Combi units also simplify maintenance. You only have one engine to service, one air filter to clean, and one spark plug to replace, instead of a separate engine for every tool. That is a real saving for small crews and owner-operators.',
            3 => 'Think about storage too. Attachments are easy to lose or damage loose in a truck bed. A simple rack or tube keeps them clean and protects the drive shafts and couplings.',
          ),
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Keeping it running',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Mix fuel fresh at the ratio in the manual and use it within a few weeks, or add stabilizer. Clean the air filter often on dusty jobs and keep the coupling free of grit so attachments seat and lock fully. Replace the trimmer line with the size Husqvarna recommends for the head.',
            1 => 'Wear eye and hearing protection, long pants, and boots. When running a pole saw attachment, also wear a helmet and stay out from under the limb you are cutting. Compare it with the larger <a href="/blowers-and-other-equipment/husqvarna-330lk-string-trimmer/">Husqvarna 330LK</a> if you need more power.',
            2 => 'Check the shaft coupling and the drive shaft splines from time to time. Worn or damaged splines cause slipping and vibration. Replace the trimmer head eyelets as they wear, and keep the cutting attachment guard in place; it limits how far debris is thrown and keeps line at the right length.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is the Husqvarna 525LK the same engine as the 525L?',
          'a' => 'Yes, both use a 25.4 cc engine. The LK has a split combi shaft and the L has a one-piece shaft.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I put a pole saw on a Husqvarna 525?',
          'a' => 'On the 525LK, yes, with a compatible Husqvarna combi pole saw attachment. The 525L\'s fixed shaft does not take attachments.',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What line size does it use?',
          'a' => 'Use the line diameter listed for the trimmer head in your operator\'s manual.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'ground',
        1 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/power-tool-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/power-tool-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Hat string trimmer',
        'creator' => 'Unknown',
        'creator_url' => '',
        'license' => 'CC0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.rawpixel.com/image/6036825/photo-image-public-domain-free-grass',
      ),
    ),
    '/blowers-and-other-equipment/husqvarna-590bts-pro-backpack-blower/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/blowers-and-other-equipment/husqvarna-590bts-pro-backpack-blower/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/blowers-and-other-equipment/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna 590BTS Pro Backpack Blower',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'power-tool',
      'price' => 749,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna 590bts backpack blower',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna 590BTS Backpack Blower: Pro Cleanup Guide',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna 590BTS Backpack Blower',
      'meta' => 'The Husqvarna 590BTS backpack blower is a high-output gas blower for clearing chips, sawdust, and leaves after tree work. Features, fit, and price.',
      'tagline' => 'High-output gas backpack blower for heavy cleanup after tree work.',
      'summary' => 'The Husqvarna 590BTS backpack blower is one of the most powerful gas backpack blowers in Husqvarna\'s professional range. Tree crews use it to clear chips, sawdust, and leaves from lawns, driveways, and roofs at the end of a job.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Top-of-range output in Husqvarna\'s backpack blowers',
        1 => 'Tube-mounted throttle for one-hand control',
        2 => 'Padded harness and back pad for all-day carry',
        3 => 'Commercial 2-stroke engine',
        4 => 'Built for heavy, wet debris and large areas',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Gas backpack blower',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Engine',
          1 => '2-stroke',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Throttle',
          1 => 'Tube-mounted',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Carry system',
          1 => 'Padded harness with hip belt',
        ),
        4 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fuel',
          1 => 'Gas and 2-stroke oil mix',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why a big blower matters on tree jobs',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Cleanup is what the customer remembers. After a removal, sawdust gets ground into the lawn, chips scatter across the driveway, and small twigs hide in landscape beds. A strong backpack blower moves all of that quickly, including damp sawdust and packed chips that a smaller handheld blower just pushes around.',
            1 => 'The 590BTS sits at the top of Husqvarna\'s backpack blower range. That extra output pays off on big properties, wet fall leaves, and storm cleanup where you are moving a lot of material in a short time.',
            2 => 'The blower also earns its keep on roofs and gutters after a crown cleaning or removal over a house. A strong blower clears leaves and twigs from shingles quickly, which saves hand work and gives the customer a clean roof. Use proper fall protection and work-positioning on any roof work.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Comfort and control',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A big blower is only useful if you can wear it for a full cleanup. The 590BTS uses a padded harness and back pad to spread the weight, and the throttle on the tube lets you feather airflow around flower beds, gravel, and mulch. Run lower throttle near loose stone and mulch and save full output for open pavement and lawn.',
            1 => 'Keep the nozzle low and work in one direction, pushing debris into a pile you can rake or vacuum up instead of blowing it into a neighbor\'s yard.',
            2 => 'Fit the harness before you start. Adjust the shoulder straps so the back pad sits flat and the weight rides on your hips, not your shoulders. Set the tube length so the nozzle reaches the ground comfortably without bending your wrist. These small adjustments matter more on a large, powerful blower than on a small one.',
            3 => 'Mind noise. Many towns have rules about gas blower use and times of day. Check local ordinances, and start blowing after the saws and chipper are done so neighbors hear the noise for the shortest time possible.',
          ),
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Ownership notes',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Husqvarna 590BTS prices vary by dealer and region; it typically costs more than mid-range blowers such as the 580BTS. Before buying, check whether a local dealer can service it, since a commercial blower will need filters, plugs, and the occasional carburetor cleaning over its life.',
            1 => 'Use fresh mixed fuel, clean the air filters often, and inspect the harness and tube clamps. Wear hearing and eye protection and a dust mask when blowing fine sawdust. Browse other <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/blowers-and-other-equipment/">blowers and power equipment</a> to round out your cleanup kit.',
            2 => 'A cleaning kit for the engine cooling fins, a spare air filter, and a spark plug on the truck will save a trip back to the shop. Inspect the harness for wear on the straps and buckles at the start of each season.',
            3 => 'Store the blower with an empty tank or stabilized fuel if it will sit for more than a few weeks. Check the tube connections for cracks before each season.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is the Husqvarna 590BTS for sale as a homeowner blower?',
          'a' => 'It can be bought by anyone, but it is a professional blower sized for commercial cleanup. Homeowners with small yards will find it more than they need.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What fuel does the 590BTS use?',
          'a' => 'Gasoline mixed with 2-stroke oil at the ratio in the operator\'s manual.',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How does it compare to a leaf blower for homeowners?',
          'a' => 'It moves far more air and is built to be serviced and run daily, with a heavier, more comfortable harness.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'ground',
        1 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/power-tool-3.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/power-tool-3-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'NCCC - Fuels Reduction',
        'creator' => 'Joshua Tree National Park',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/115357548@N08',
        'license' => 'Public domain',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/115357548@N08/51765717788',
      ),
    ),
    '/blowers-and-other-equipment/husqvarna-k970-power-cutter/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/blowers-and-other-equipment/husqvarna-k970-power-cutter/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/blowers-and-other-equipment/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna K970 Power Cutter',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'power-tool',
      'price' => 1649,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna k970',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna K970 Power Cutter: Specs, Uses & Price',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna K970 Power Cutter',
      'meta' => 'The Husqvarna K970 is a 93.6 cc gas power cutter for concrete, stone, and steel. Blade sizes, where it helps tree crews, safety notes, and typical price.',
      'tagline' => 'Heavy-duty 93.6 cc gas cut-off saw for concrete, stone, and metal.',
      'summary' => 'The Husqvarna K970 is a heavy-duty gas power cutter with a 93.6 cc engine, built for cutting concrete, stone, asphalt, and steel. Tree and site crews reach for the K970 saw when roots run under hardscape or a removal needs a curb, slab, or pipe cut.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => '93.6 cc 2-stroke engine',
        1 => 'Takes 14 in blades, with a 16 in model available',
        2 => 'Wet cutting kit to control dust',
        3 => 'Active air filtration for dusty work',
        4 => 'Built for daily commercial use',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Displacement',
          1 => '93.6 cc',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Engine',
          1 => '2-stroke',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Blade size',
          1 => '14 in (16 in version available)',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Dust control',
          1 => 'Water kit for wet cutting',
        ),
        4 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fuel',
          1 => 'Gas and 2-stroke oil mix',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Where a power cutter fits a tree business',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Most arborists never need a cut-off saw until the day they do. Roots heave a sidewalk and the city wants the slab cut back. A stump sits against a curb or a retaining wall. Storm cleanup leaves a steel fence or pipe tangled in a trunk. The K970 handles those jobs, cutting concrete, stone, asphalt, and steel with the right blade.',
            1 => 'It is also a common rental-yard and contractor saw, so crews who do hardscape or site prep alongside tree work often own one.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Engine and blades',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The 93.6 cc engine gives the K970 the power to keep blade speed up in thick concrete without bogging. The standard model runs a 14 in blade, and a 16 in version gives a deeper cut. Choose a diamond blade matched to the material: a general-purpose concrete blade for slabs and curbs, an asphalt blade for paving, and an abrasive or diamond blade rated for steel when cutting metal.',
            1 => 'Always check that the blade\'s maximum RPM rating is above the saw\'s spindle speed and that the arbor fits.',
            2 => 'Diamond blades last much longer than abrasive wheels in concrete and stone and keep a more consistent cutting depth as they wear. Abrasive wheels still have a place for steel and occasional jobs, but wear down quickly and need to be checked for damage before every use.',
          ),
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Dust, kickback, and safe use',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Cutting concrete and stone releases respirable crystalline silica. Use the water kit for wet cutting, follow OSHA\'s silica rules, and wear a respirator when required. Add eye and face protection, hearing protection, gloves, and sturdy boots.',
            1 => 'Power cutters can kick back and climb if the blade pinches or the top quadrant contacts the work. Cut with the lower part of the blade, support the work so the kerf opens rather than closes, and keep bystanders out of the spark and debris path. Read the operator\'s manual and get trained before running one.',
            2 => 'Never cut with the blade above shoulder height, and do not use the K970 on a ladder. Start the saw on the ground with the blade clear, and let it reach full speed before entering the cut.',
          ),
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Price and upkeep',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The K970 typically sells for around $1,600 to $1,700 as a bare saw, usually without a diamond blade. Budget for blades, the water kit if not included, filters, and spare plugs. Keep the air filters clean, since dust is the main enemy of a cut-off saw engine. See the rest of our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/blowers-and-other-equipment/">power equipment</a> for jobsite tools.',
            1 => 'If you only need a power cutter a few times a year, renting may make more sense than owning. If your crew regularly handles root and hardscape conflicts, owning the K970 saves time and rental costs.',
            2 => 'Write down the blade type and hours on each blade so you know when to replace it, and store blades flat in a dry place to keep them true.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What size blade does the Husqvarna K970 take?',
          'a' => 'The standard K970 takes a 14 in blade. A 16 in version is available for deeper cuts.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can the K970 saw cut roots?',
          'a' => 'It is not designed for wood. Use a chainsaw or root saw for roots and the K970 for concrete, stone, and steel.',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is the K970 good for wet cutting?',
          'a' => 'Yes. Use the water kit to control silica dust when cutting concrete or stone.',
        ),
      ),
