    '/climbing/spurs/buckingham-steel-spurs/buckingham-steel-climbers-with-t-pads/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/climbing/spurs/buckingham-steel-spurs/buckingham-steel-climbers-with-t-pads/',
      'category' => '/climbing/spurs/buckingham-steel-spurs/',
      'name' => 'Buckingham Steel Climbers with T-Pads',
      'brand' => 'buckingham',
      'brand_name' => 'Buckingham',
      'kind' => 'spur',
      'price' => 279,
      'keyword' => 'buckingham tree spikes',
      'title' => 'Buckingham Tree Spikes with T-Pads (Steel Climbers)',
      'h1' => 'Buckingham Tree Spikes: Steel Climbers with T-Pads',
      'meta' => 'Buckingham tree spikes with steel shanks and classic T-pads: a lighter, simpler upper on tough steel climbers. Typical price, fit advice and gaff care tips.',
      'tagline' => 'Steel Buckingham tree spikes with traditional T-pad uppers for removal climbers.',
      'summary' => 'These Buckingham tree spikes combine steel shanks with T-pads, a traditional upper that is lighter and less bulky than wide wrap pads. Many climbers like the T-pad for its simple, close fit and easy strap adjustment.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Steel shanks for long service life',
        1 => 'T-pad uppers with a close, low-bulk fit',
        2 => 'Replaceable gaffs',
        3 => 'Adjustable shank length',
        4 => 'Pairs well with stiff steel-shank climbing boots',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Shank material',
          1 => 'Steel',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Pad style',
          1 => 'T-pads',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Gaffs',
          1 => 'Replaceable tree gaffs',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fit',
          1 => 'Adjustable shank length',
        ),
        4 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Intended use',
          1 => 'Tree removal',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'A classic setup',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The T-pad is the traditional upper on Buckingham spikes. It is a T-shaped pad that sits against the calf with a strap around the leg. It carries less bulk than a full wrap pad, so it packs smaller and feels less hot in summer.',
            1 => 'Paired with steel shanks, these Buckingham climbing spikes are a durable, straightforward removal set. If you want more comfort for long days, look at the Big Buck pad version in our <a href="/climbing/spurs/buckingham-steel-spurs/">Buckingham steel spurs</a> lineup.',
            2 => 'Steel shanks are the practical choice for crews that share gear or climbers who only spike a few removals a month. They cost less than aluminum and handle rough storage, so Buckingham tree spikes like these can live in the truck and still be ready when the next removal comes in.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Boots matter',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Spurs only work as well as the boot under them. Look for tree climbing boots with a steel shank in the sole and good ankle support. The stirrup sits under the arch, and a stiff sole keeps it from bending your foot on every step.',
            1 => 'Snug the lower strap around the boot so the stirrup cannot slide, and set the upper strap firm but not tight enough to cut off circulation. Adjust shank length so the top sits just below the bend in your knee.',
            2 => 'If your feet hurt after a day on spurs, look at the boot before the spur. Tree climbing boots with a steel shank spread the stirrup load across the sole, and a boot with a defined heel keeps the stirrup from sliding forward.',
          ),
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Keeping them in shape',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Sharpen gaffs with a file along the factory bevel and keep the point sharp enough to bite without a hard kick. Replace gaffs that are short, chipped or bent. Check pads and straps for wear, cuts and cracked leather.',
            1 => 'Climbing spurs are part of your fall-protection system. Inspect gaffs, shanks, straps and pads before every climb, follow the manufacturer\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, and get trained before you climb on spikes. Spurs belong on removals and rescues only; climb live trees on rope.',
            2 => 'Keep gaff guards on whenever the spurs are off your legs, both to protect the points and to keep a sharp gaff away from your rope and the truck seats.',
          ),
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Working a removal on spikes',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'On a removal, set your flip line around the stem before you start climbing and keep it adjusted so you can lean back into it. Climb with short, deliberate steps and set each gaff at a slight angle into the wood rather than flat against the bark.',
            1 => 'When you reach your work position, set a second attachment before you start the saw. Spurs give you footing, but your lanyard and climbing line hold you. Rest often on long climbs; tired legs lead to sloppy kicks and cut-outs.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Are T-pads comfortable?',
          'a' => 'They are comfortable for many climbers, especially on shorter climbs. For all-day removals, wider pads like Big Buck pads spread load better.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Do I need special boots for tree spikes?',
          'a' => 'Use a stiff work or climbing boot with a steel shank in the sole. Soft hikers or sneakers are not suitable.',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I upgrade the pads later?',
          'a' => 'Yes. Uppers are replaceable, so you can move to Big Buck pads without replacing the climbers.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/buckingham/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/spur-5.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/spur-5-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'TVCF003',
        'creator' => 'Symic',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/73344134@N00',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/73344134@N00/33549423240',
      ),
    ),
    '/climbing/spurs/climber-pads/buckingham-big-buck-pads/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/climbing/spurs/climber-pads/buckingham-big-buck-pads/',
      'category' => '/climbing/spurs/climber-pads/',
      'name' => 'Buckingham Big Buck Pads',
      'brand' => 'buckingham',
      'brand_name' => 'Buckingham',
      'kind' => 'spur',
      'price' => 139,
      'keyword' => 'buckingham big buck pads',
      'title' => 'Buckingham Big Buck Pads for Climbing Spurs',
      'h1' => 'Buckingham Big Buck Pads',
      'meta' => 'Buckingham Big Buck pads are wide, padded uppers for buck spur climbers. Spread load across the calf and steady the shank on long removals. Typical price here.',
      'tagline' => 'Wide, padded replacement uppers that make long days on spurs easier on your calves.',
      'summary' => 'Buckingham Big Buck pads are wide replacement uppers for climbing spurs that spread pressure across the calf and keep the shank steady. They are a common upgrade for climbers whose stock pads dig in after an hour on the stem.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Wide padded upper spreads pressure',
        1 => 'Holds the spur steady against the leg',
        2 => 'Replaces worn or narrow pads',
        3 => 'Buckle strap closure',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Replacement upper pads',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Closure',
          1 => 'Buckle straps',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Sold as',
          1 => 'Pair',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why upgrade your pads',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Pads take the load when you stand in your spurs. Narrow or worn pads concentrate that load and leave bruises on the calf. Big Buck pads use a wider padded shell that wraps more of the leg, and the stiffer shape helps the buck spur stay aligned so the gaff bites cleanly.',
            1 => 'They are a common upgrade for <a href="/climbing/spurs/buckingham-steel-spurs/">Buckingham steel spurs</a> and other compatible climbers.',
            2 => 'New pads are also cheaper than new climbers. If your shanks and gaffs are in good shape, replacing the uppers is often all it takes to make an old pair feel new. The buckle closure is easy to adjust with gloves and holds firm through a full day of kicking in on removals.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fit and inspection',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Confirm the pads fit your climber model before ordering. Mount them so the top of the pad sits below the bend in the knee and the straps close snug without pinching. Inspect stitching, buckles and padding before each climb, and replace pads that are cracked or torn. Spurs are life-support gear: follow the manufacturer\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, and be trained before climbing.',
            1 => 'Keep a pair of gaff guards on your spurs during storage so the points do not cut into the new pads or straps.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will Big Buck pads fit my spurs?',
          'a' => 'They are made for Buckingham climbers and some compatible models. Check the fit information before you buy.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Buckle or hook-and-loop?',
          'a' => 'This is the buckle version. A hook-and-loop closure version is also available for faster on and off.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/buckingham/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/spur-0.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/spur-0-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Wood pole ascent',
        'creator' => 'Western Area Power Admin',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/86561000@N05',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/86561000@N05/16380468763',
      ),
    ),
    '/climbing/spurs/climber-pads/buckingham-big-buck-velcro-pads/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/climbing/spurs/climber-pads/buckingham-big-buck-velcro-pads/',
      'category' => '/climbing/spurs/climber-pads/',
      'name' => 'Buckingham Big Buck Velcro Pads',
      'brand' => 'buckingham',
      'brand_name' => 'Buckingham',
      'kind' => 'spur',
      'price' => 149,
      'keyword' => 'buckingham big buck pads',
      'title' => 'Buckingham Big Buck Pads with Hook-and-Loop Closure',
      'h1' => 'Buckingham Big Buck Pads, Velcro Closure',
      'meta' => 'Buckingham Big Buck pads with a hook-and-loop closure: wide, padded spur uppers that go on and off fast between climbs. Fit notes and typical price inside.',
      'tagline' => 'Wide Big Buck uppers with a quick hook-and-loop closure for fast on and off.',
      'summary' => 'These Buckingham Big Buck pads use a hook-and-loop closure instead of buckles, so you can strap in and out of your spurs quickly. You still get the wide, padded upper that spreads load across the calf.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Wide Big Buck pad shape',
        1 => 'Hook-and-loop closure for quick adjustment',
        2 => 'Spreads load and steadies the shank',
        3 => 'Replaces worn uppers',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Replacement upper pads',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Closure',
          1 => 'Hook-and-loop',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Sold as',
          1 => 'Pair',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fast on, fast off',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'On jobs where you go up and down several trees, buckles slow you down. The hook-and-loop closure on these Big Buck pads lets you snug the upper in one move and pull it off just as fast. The wide padded shell still wraps the calf to reduce pressure points and keep the spur aligned.',
            1 => 'Shop other <a href="/climbing/spurs/climber-pads/">climber pads</a> if you prefer a buckle closure.',
            2 => 'That speed is useful on lot clearing and storm work, where you might top and drop several trees in a morning. It also makes it easier to loosen the upper during a break on the ground, which helps circulation on long days on spikes.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Keep the closure clean',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Hook-and-loop loses grip when packed with sawdust, bark and pitch. Brush it clean regularly and replace pads when the closure no longer holds firmly. Check fit with your climber model before ordering. Inspect pads and straps before every climb, follow the manufacturer\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, and be trained before climbing on spurs.',
            1 => 'If you climb in wet, muddy or icy conditions often, consider the buckle version, which is less affected by debris. Many climbers keep one of each and choose by the job. Store spurs with gaff guards on so points cannot catch the closure.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is hook-and-loop as secure as buckles?',
          'a' => 'When clean and in good condition it holds well. Debris weakens it, so keep it clean and replace pads when grip fades.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Do these fit all spurs?',
          'a' => 'They are designed for Buckingham climbers and some compatible models. Confirm fit before ordering.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/buckingham/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/spur-1.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/spur-1-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Wood pole ascent',
        'creator' => 'Western Area Power Admin',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/86561000@N05',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/86561000@N05/16814256419',
      ),
    ),
    '/climbing/spurs/replacement-gaffs-and-parts/buckalloy-screw-and-dowel-style-replacement-tree-gaffs/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/climbing/spurs/replacement-gaffs-and-parts/buckalloy-screw-and-dowel-style-replacement-tree-gaffs/',
      'category' => '/climbing/spurs/replacement-gaffs-and-parts/',
      'name' => 'Buckingham Buckalloy Screw and Dowel Style Replacement Tree Gaffs',
      'brand' => 'buckingham',
      'brand_name' => 'Buckingham',
      'kind' => 'spur',
      'price' => 89,
      'keyword' => 'buckingham replacement gaffs',
      'title' => 'Buckingham Replacement Gaffs: Buckalloy Screw and Dowel',
      'h1' => 'Buckingham Replacement Gaffs: Buckalloy Screw and Dowel Style',
      'meta' => 'Buckingham replacement gaffs in Buckalloy, screw and dowel style: fresh tree gaffs for worn spurs. When to replace gaffs and how to fit them. Typical price.',
      'tagline' => 'Screw and dowel style Buckalloy tree gaffs to bring worn Buckingham spurs back.',
      'summary' => 'These Buckingham replacement gaffs are Buckalloy tree gaffs in the screw and dowel mounting style. Swap them in when your old gaffs are short, chipped or bent and get a confident bite back without buying new climbers.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Screw and dowel mounting style',
        1 => 'Tree-length gaffs for bark penetration',
        2 => 'Restores worn climbers',
        3 => 'Made for Buckingham-style shanks',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Material',
          1 => 'Buckalloy',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Mount',
          1 => 'Screw and dowel',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Tree gaffs',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'When to replace gaffs',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Gaffs wear every time you sharpen them. Once they get short, the point no longer reaches through thick bark, and that is when cut-outs happen. Replace gaffs that are shortened past the maker\'s limit, chipped, cracked or bent. Do not try to straighten a bent gaff.',
            1 => 'Match the mount style to your climbers. These are screw and dowel style; check your shanks before ordering from <a href="/climbing/spurs/replacement-gaffs-and-parts/">replacement gaffs and parts</a>.',
            2 => 'A fresh set of Buckingham replacement gaffs is one of the cheapest ways to make old climbers feel safer. Sharp, full-length gaffs set with a lighter kick, so you climb with less effort and less strain on your knees and ankles.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting and sharpening',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Install gaffs following the manufacturer\'s instructions and tighten the screws firmly. Sharpen with a file along the factory bevel and never on a grinder, which can overheat the metal. Spurs are life-support equipment: inspect before every climb, follow ANSI Z133, and be trained before climbing on spikes.',
            1 => 'Always replace gaffs as a pair so both legs bite the same way. Keep gaff guards on whenever the spurs are off your legs to protect the new points and everything around them.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will these fit my spurs?',
          'a' => 'They fit climbers that use screw and dowel style gaffs. Confirm your shank type before buying.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I sharpen gaffs on a bench grinder?',
          'a' => 'No. Heat can ruin the temper. Use a file and follow the original bevel.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
        1 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/buckingham/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/spur-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/spur-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Fall Protection Training, 2013',
        'creator' => 'Western Area Power Admin',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/86561000@N05',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/86561000@N05/8813825794',
      ),
    ),
    '/climbing/spurs/replacement-gaffs-and-parts/edelrid-talon-upper-strap-system/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/climbing/spurs/replacement-gaffs-and-parts/edelrid-talon-upper-strap-system/',
      'category' => '/climbing/spurs/replacement-gaffs-and-parts/',
      'name' => 'Edelrid Talon Upper Strap System',
      'brand' => 'edelrid',
      'brand_name' => 'Edelrid',
      'kind' => 'spur',
      'price' => 99,
      'keyword' => 'edelrid talons',
      'title' => 'Upper Strap System for Edelrid Talons',
      'h1' => 'Upper Strap System for Edelrid Talons',
      'meta' => 'Replacement upper strap system for Edelrid Talon spurs. Refresh worn uppers on your Edelrid Talons and keep the climber snug and steady. Typical price and tips.',
      'tagline' => 'Replacement upper straps and pads for Edelrid Talon climbing spurs.',
      'summary' => 'The upper strap system for Edelrid Talons lets you refresh worn straps and padding without replacing the spurs. A fresh upper keeps the shank steady and comfortable on long removals.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Made for Edelrid Talon spurs',
        1 => 'Restores a snug, steady fit',
        2 => 'Replaces worn or damaged uppers',
        3 => 'Keeps your spurs in service longer',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Compatible with',
          1 => 'Edelrid Talon spurs',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Upper strap system',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Replaces',
          1 => 'Worn Talon upper straps and padding',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Refresh your Talons',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Uppers wear out faster than shanks. Padding packs down, straps fray and closures lose grip. Swapping in a new upper strap system restores the fit that keeps the gaff angle consistent and your calf comfortable.',
            1 => 'Find gaffs and other parts in <a href="/climbing/spurs/replacement-gaffs-and-parts/">replacement gaffs and parts</a>.',
            2 => 'Edelrid Talons are popular with removal climbers who want a modern, adjustable spur, and the upper is the part that takes the most wear. Sweat, sawdust, bark and pitch all break down padding and straps over a season of hard use. Rather than living with a sloppy fit, replace the upper and get back the support the spur had when it was new.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Install and inspect',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Install the system following Edelrid\'s instructions and check that every strap closes securely before climbing. Inspect uppers, lower straps, shanks and gaffs before every climb. Spurs are life-support gear: follow the manufacturer\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, and be trained before you climb on spikes.',
            1 => 'Keep the old upper as a reference while installing the new one, so straps go back in the same orientation. Store your Talons with gaff guards on, and keep the new upper away from fuel, bar oil and solvents.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does this fit other spurs?',
          'a' => 'It is made for Edelrid Talon spurs. Do not mix it with other brands unless the manufacturer says it is compatible.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'When should I replace the upper?',
          'a' => 'Replace it when padding is packed flat, straps are cut or frayed, or closures no longer hold firmly.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
        1 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
