          1 => 'Arborwear',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Tech fabric for working warm',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Cotton holds sweat, and wet cotton gets cold fast when you stop working. The Tech Double Thick uses a technical fabric that moves moisture better, so you stay warmer through the climb-sweat-stop cycle of tree work.',
            1 => 'If you are searching for Arborwear near me, you can compare this pullover with the rest of our <a href="/clothing/sweatshirts-and-jackets/">sweatshirts and jackets</a> online.',
            2 => 'The double-layer build gives you warmth on cold mornings while the technical fabric dries faster than heavy cotton fleece. That makes it a good choice for climbers who work hard and sweat, then stand around on the ground while the crew cleans up. It is also lighter to wear under a saddle than a thick cotton hoodie.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Visibility',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Safety yellow helps the ground crew track the climber and makes you easier to see around trucks and equipment. A colored sweatshirt is not certified high-visibility clothing, so wear an approved vest on roadside jobs as your traffic plan requires. Keep clothing snug near chippers and follow ANSI Z133.',
            1 => 'Wash cold and hang dry or tumble dry low, and skip fabric softener so the fabric keeps moving moisture. Bright colors show dirt, so wash it regularly to keep it visible.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is this a high-visibility garment?',
          'a' => 'It is a bright color, but it is not certified high-visibility apparel. Use an approved vest where required.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How should I wash it?',
          'a' => 'Wash cold and hang dry or tumble dry low. Skip fabric softener.',
        ),
      ),
