          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Samson Rope',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'The middle size most crews need',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A 5/8 in line handles the pieces that are too big for a 1/2 in rope but do not justify hauling out the 3/4 in. It is a good default for removals on residential lots where you are lowering leaders and trunk sections of moderate size.',
            1 => 'A 200 ft of rope length gives plenty of reach from a high block to a lowering device at the base, with tail for the groundie.',
            2 => 'Samson Stable Braid has a firm, round build that keeps its shape on a capstan or bollard, so the groundie gets predictable friction when letting a piece run. Crews often pair a 5/8 rope with a matching block and sling for medium removals.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Use and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Plan the rigging, account for shock loading, and stay within the manufacturer\'s rated values and ANSI Z133. A trained crew member should set up every rigging system.',
            1 => 'Inspect the cover and feel for flat or stiff spots before each use. Keep it out of fuel and bar oil, flake it into a bag, and retire it if it is damaged. Never use rigging rope for climbing.',
            2 => 'Rotate which end you use for the block so wear does not concentrate in one spot, and spliced eyes should be checked closely since they take a lot of the load.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is 5/8 rope good for tree rigging?',
          'a' => 'Yes. It is a common middle size that handles medium-to-heavy wood. Match it to the load and your block and sling.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How long is a typical Stable Braid rigging line?',
          'a' => '200 ft is popular for rigging because it reaches from a high block to the ground with room to spare. Check the listing for available lengths.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
