          0 => 'Use',
          1 => 'Climbing line (SRS and MRS)',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'How Vesper climbs',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Vesper is built with low stretch in mind, so foot-lock and rope-walker ascents put more of each step into height and less into bouncing. On descent it feeds smoothly through common SRS devices, and at 11.8mm it holds a matching friction hitch well when you switch to moving rope work.',
            1 => 'The blue and orange pattern is bold enough to pick out against bark, sky and green leaves, which helps a ground worker follow your line and helps you sort your own rope from a crew\'s shared lines.',
            2 => 'Blue and orange also contrast well with most rigging lines, so a groundie can tell at a glance which rope is the climber\'s lifeline and keep clear of it when pulling brush.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Setup and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Check that your device lists 11.8mm rope as compatible, and test any hitch pairing near the ground. Low-stretch line passes shock straight through the system, so keep slack out and never use a climbing line for rigging.',
            1 => 'Climbing line is life-support equipment. Use it only within the manufacturer\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, inspect it before every climb, retire it when the cover is cut or glazed or the core feels damaged, and get proper training before you trust it. Compare other <a href="/rope/climbing-rope/24-strand-climbing-rope/">24-strand climbing rope</a> in our range.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What diameter is Marlow Vesper?',
          'a' => 'Vesper is an 11.8mm arborist climbing line.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is the Blue/Orange Vesper different from other colors?',
          'a' => 'The color is the main difference. Check the listing for length and any spliced eye before you order.',
