        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/35518575@N00/5198346327',
      ),
    ),
    '/auto-locking-carabiners/camp-oval-xl-3lock-carabiner/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/auto-locking-carabiners/camp-oval-xl-3lock-carabiner/',
      'category' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/carabiners-and-hardware/auto-locking-carabiners/',
      'name' => 'CAMP Oval XL 3Lock Carabiner',
      'brand' => 'camp',
      'brand_name' => 'CAMP',
      'kind' => 'carabiner',
      'price' => 24,
      'keyword' => 'camp oval xl 3lock',
      'title' => 'CAMP Oval XL 3Lock Carabiner: Triple-Lock Oval',
      'h1' => 'CAMP Oval XL 3Lock Carabiner',
      'meta' => 'CAMP Oval XL 3Lock: a large aluminum oval carabiner with a triple-action auto-locking gate, made for pulleys, hitch systems and gear-heavy arborist setups.',
      'tagline' => 'A large aluminum oval with a triple-action auto-lock gate for pulleys and devices.',
      'summary' => 'The CAMP Oval XL 3Lock carabiner is a large aluminum oval with a triple-action auto-locking gate. Its symmetrical shape keeps pulleys, rope wrenches and hitch systems sitting square, and the bigger size makes room for several items.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Oval shape keeps pulleys centered',
        1 => 'XL size for multiple items',
        2 => 'Triple-action auto-locking gate',
        3 => 'Lightweight aluminum',
        4 => 'Easy to work with gloves',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Material',
          1 => 'Aluminum',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Shape',
          1 => 'Oval',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Gate',
          1 => 'Triple-action auto-locking',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why an oval',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'An oval\'s symmetrical shape lets a pulley or device sit in the middle of the basket instead of sliding to one side. That keeps loading even and stops pulleys from twisting, which is why ovals are a common choice for hitch climbing systems, micro pulleys and rope-wrench setups.',
            1 => 'The XL size gives extra room for a pulley plus a hitch tender or a second connector, and it is easier to handle with gloves. The triple-action gate needs a twist and push to open, so it resists accidental opening against bark and rope.',
            2 => 'Aluminum ovals wear where rope or pulley sideplates rub, so look for grooves or sharp edges at the ends of the basket. Many climbers keep one XL oval as the backbone of their hitch system and replace it on a schedule. Keep it out of the saw bucket and away from bar oil and fuel, which make gates sticky.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Use and inspection',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Ovals are generally rated lower than D shapes because the load sits further from the spine, so check the strength markings on the carabiner and make sure it suits your system.',
            1 => 'Carabiners in a climbing system are life-support gear. Use only connectors rated for the purpose, follow ANSI Z133 and the maker\'s instructions, load them along the major axis, and inspect the gate, spring and body before each use. Compare more <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/carabiners-and-hardware/auto-locking-carabiners/">auto-locking carabiners</a>.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What is the CAMP Oval XL 3Lock good for?',
          'a' => 'Holding pulleys, hitch systems and devices centered, with room for multiple items.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is a triple-lock gate required for climbing?',
          'a' => 'Follow ANSI Z133, your employer\'s rules and the device maker\'s instructions. Many arborists prefer triple-action gates for life support.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/camp/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/carabiner-4.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/carabiner-4-sm.webp',
        'title' => '3D-printed Carabiner Clip',
        'creator' => 'Creative Tools',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/33907867@N02',
