            2 => 'Because compact ovals have less room, they suit dedicated setups where the same pulley and hitch stay together. Keep the gate clean, rinse grit out after muddy climbs, and retire the carabiner if it is dropped onto a hard surface from height, shows grooves, or the gate fails to close and lock on its own.',
