      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why climbers wear saw pants',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Chaps work well on the ground, but they flap, catch and get hot when you climb. Saw pants put the cut-resistant layers into the trouser itself, so there is nothing loose to snag on a limb or your saddle.',
            1 => 'The BreatheFlex Pro is Arbortec\'s lighter, more breathable line, made for long days and hot weather. This version pairs Realtree camo with brown accents. Compare colors and fits in <a href="/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chaps-and-protective-gear/chainsaw-pants/">chainsaw pants</a>.',
            2 => 'On a removal you might climb, cut, rappel and then drag brush for an hour, all in the same pants. That is where a light, stretchy saw pant pays off. You are not taking chaps on and off between jobs, and you are less likely to skip protection because it is too hot.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fit, rating and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Check the label for the protection type and class, and make sure it meets what your employer and ANSI Z133 call for on your work. Saw protection only works if it fits, so choose a size that covers you without bunching.',
            1 => 'Wash as Arbortec instructs. Any cut that reaches the protective layer means the pants are done and should be replaced, not patched.',
            2 => 'Saw protection reduces injury risk but does not make you cut-proof. Keep a sharp chain, a working chain brake, good footing and two hands on the saw whenever you can. Pair the pants with saw boots, gloves, a helmet with face screen and hearing protection.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Are the BreatheFlex Pro pants good for climbing?',
          'a' => 'Yes. They are designed to be light and flexible enough to climb in while still giving saw protection.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I repair cut chainsaw pants?',
          'a' => 'No. If a cut reaches the protective layer, replace the pants.',
        ),
      ),
