          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Edelrid',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Use',
          1 => 'Rope ascent',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'What it does',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'On a single rope, most of the effort is in the ascent. A foot-worn aid like the Talon grips the rope as you step and slides as you lift, turning the climb into a steady walk.',
            1 => 'It pairs with a hand ascender and a proper SRS system. Check Edelrid\'s instructions for the rope diameters and setup it is designed for. Related gear is in <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/ascent-and-descent/foot-ascenders-and-foot-loops/">foot ascenders and foot loops</a>.',
            2 => 'Foot-worn ascent aids are popular with climbers who work tall trees or do several climbs a day, since saving energy on the way up leaves more for the work at the top. Talk to a trainer about how it fits your system.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Setup and inspection',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Fit it to your boot as Edelrid describes and practice low before going high.',
            1 => 'It is an ascent aid only, not life support. Life-support gear must meet the applicable standard (ANSI Z133 and the manufacturer\'s instructions), be inspected before every use, and be used only by trained climbers. Check the cam, spring and straps before every climb.',
            2 => 'Keep the device clean of sap and bark so it grips evenly. Store it in your climbing bag where it will not be crushed or bent, and replace straps or worn parts according to Edelrid\'s guidance.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is the Edelrid Talon a life-support device?',
          'a' => 'No. It is an ascent aid and must be used alongside a proper life-support connection.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What rope does the Talon work with?',
