        3 => 'Keeps pulleys centered',
        4 => 'Made by DMM',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Shape',
          1 => 'Large oval',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Gate',
          1 => 'Locksafe three-stage auto-locking',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'DMM',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why climbers pick it',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The Ultra O has more room inside than most ovals, so it works well when you need several items in one carabiner, such as a micro pulley and a hitch cord eye, or a ring and a sling. The symmetric shape lets those pieces settle in the middle instead of sliding toward the gate.',
            1 => 'Locksafe is DMM\'s three-stage gate: twist, push up, then open. It takes a moment to learn, but it is very hard for a branch, rope, or bark to open it by accident. That is a sensible trade on a connector that sits in the middle of your climbing system.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Inspection and retirement',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Before each climb, open the gate and let it snap shut. It should close fully and lock on its own without sticking. Look for cracks, sharp edges, grooves worn by rope, and deformation at the nose or hinge. Sap and grit are the usual cause of a lazy gate, so rinse and dry the carabiner and keep the gate mechanism clean.',
            1 => 'Retire any carabiner that has been dropped from height onto a hard surface, shock loaded, or shows wear you cannot explain. Read the markings on the spine and confirm they meet what your system needs. Life-support gear must meet the applicable standard (ANSI Z133 and the manufacturer\'s instructions), be inspected before every climb, and be used only by trained climbers. See more <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/carabiners-and-hardware/auto-locking-carabiners/">auto-locking carabiners</a>.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do you open a Locksafe gate?',
          'a' => 'Twist the sleeve, push it up toward the nose, then open the gate. It relocks when released.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is the Ultra O good with a micro pulley?',
          'a' => 'Yes. The oval shape keeps a pulley centered, which is why it is a common pairing.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
        1 => 'rigging',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/dmm/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/carabiner-3.webp',
