          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Climb Right adjustable steel climbers',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Includes',
          1 => 'Adjustment sleeve and screws',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Material',
          1 => 'Steel',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why the sleeve matters',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The sleeve sets how high the shank rides on your leg. Too high and it digs in behind the knee every time you bend; too low and the spur feels loose and less stable. When holes elongate or screws strip, you lose that adjustment and the spur can shift.',
            1 => 'Check your climber model before ordering. More Climb Right and other parts are in <a href="/climbing/spurs/replacement-gaffs-and-parts/">replacement gaffs and parts</a>.',
            2 => 'When you order parts, note your climber brand, model and roughly when you bought it. Makers revise designs over the years, and that detail is the fastest way to be sure the replacement matches what is on your spurs.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Installing it',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Remove the old sleeve, fit the new one with the supplied screws and tighten firmly. Set height with your work boot on so the top of the shank sits a little below the knee, then confirm nothing moves under load.',
            1 => 'After any repair, inspect the whole spur before climbing. Follow the manufacturer\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, and have a qualified person check the work if you are unsure.',
            2 => 'Spur parts are cheap next to a fall or a lost day. Keep a small kit in the climbing bag with a file, a gauge, spare screws and a strap, so a worn part gets swapped at the truck instead of nursed through the rest of the job.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Are screws included?',
          'a' => 'Yes, this kit includes the sleeve and the screws.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will it fit Climb Right aluminum climbers?',
          'a' => 'It is listed for Climb Right steel climbers. Check your model before ordering.',
        ),
      ),
