        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Where it fits and where it does not',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A ball cap is for ground work, travel and the shop. It is not head protection. When you climb, run a saw, work under a climber or stand in the drop zone, wear a helmet that meets the standard your employer and ANSI Z133 require, and keep the cap in the truck.',
            1 => 'Hand wash with mild soap and cool water and let it air dry on its own shape. A washing machine can bend the brim and break down the front panel. Rinse sweat and sap out after summer work so the mesh stays soft and the band does not stiffen.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I wear a trucker hat under my climbing helmet?',
          'a' => 'Generally no. A cap brim can change how a helmet sits and fits. Follow your helmet maker\'s instructions; most allow only a thin liner or nothing at all.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I clean a mesh trucker hat?',
          'a' => 'Hand wash in cool water with mild soap, rinse well and air dry. Avoid the dryer and the washing machine, which can warp the brim.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'apparel',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/gap-arborist-supply/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/apparel-1.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/apparel-1-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Flannel plaid background',
