          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Arborwear',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'The heavy-duty climbing pant',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The Original Tree Climbers\' Pants are the heavy canvas option in the Arborwear lineup. The fabric is stiff out of the bag and breaks in over a few weeks of climbing and washing. In exchange you get a pant that stands up to spurs on bark, rope over the knee and long days dragging brush.',
            1 => 'A gusseted crotch adds room so you can step high without the seam pulling. Chestnut is a warm brown that hides dirt and sap. If you prefer stretch, compare the lighter options on our <a href="/clothing/tree-climbing-pants/">tree climbing pants</a> page.',
            2 => 'They suit climbers who do a lot of spur work on removals, crews in brushy country and anyone who finds lighter stretch pants wear through at the knee within a season. In summer heat they feel warm, which is the price of the heavier fabric.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fit, care and limits',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Heavy cotton can shrink a little in hot water, so wash cold and dry low or hang dry. Order your usual size and expect a stiff feel at first. Make sure pockets do not sit under saddle leg loops.',
            1 => 'These are work pants, not chainsaw protection. When you run a saw on the ground, wear chaps or chainsaw-protective pants as ANSI Z133 requires. Check the seams and knees as they age and patch wear early.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Are the Original Tree Climbers\' Pants stiff?',
          'a' => 'Yes, at first. Heavy canvas softens with washing and wear over a few weeks.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Do they protect against chainsaw cuts?',
          'a' => 'No. Wear chaps or chainsaw pants when running a saw on the ground.',
        ),
      ),
