      'keyword' => 'notch pro access bag',
      'title' => 'Notch Pro Access Bag for Climbing Gear',
      'h1' => 'Notch Pro Access Bag',
      'meta' => 'The Notch Pro Access bag carries climbing gear with easy access on the job. See how arborists use it, what it suits, and how to keep life-support gear clean.',
      'tagline' => 'A Notch gear bag for keeping climbing kit organized and easy to reach.',
      'summary' => 'The Notch Pro Access bag is a gear bag for arborists who want their climbing kit organized and quick to get at on the job. Notch makes a wide range of tree climbing gear and accessories, and this bag is built for daily use.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Gear bag from Notch',
        1 => 'Designed for quick access to kit',
        2 => 'Keeps climbing gear separate and clean',
        3 => 'Built for daily job-site use',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Notch',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Gear bag',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Organized kit, faster setup',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'On a busy job, digging for a carabiner or hitch cord wastes time. A bag that opens wide makes it easy to see your kit, check it, and get climbing. It also makes the end-of-day check simple: everything goes back where it came from.',
            1 => 'Use it for climbing gear, or as a dedicated bag for rigging hardware if you keep the two kits apart.',
            2 => 'For crews that share kit, a dedicated bag per climber helps prevent gear from getting mixed up. Each climber knows their own saddle, hitch cords, and hardware, and knows the history of each piece. That makes inspection and retirement decisions much easier.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Keep the bag away from fuel and bar oil, shake out sawdust, and dry it open after wet days. Check your gear as you pack and unpack it.',
            1 => 'Clean the bag out regularly. Sawdust, sap, and grit work into hardware and soft goods, and a quick shake-out at the end of the week keeps your kit easier to inspect.',
            2 => 'See other <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/gear-storage/gear-bags/">gear bags</a>. Life-support gear must meet the applicable standard (ANSI Z133 and the manufacturer\'s instructions), be inspected before every use, and be used only by trained climbers.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What fits in the Notch Pro Access bag?',
          'a' => 'Check the listing for capacity. Gear bags like this are generally sized for a saddle, hardware, and small lines.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Should my climbing rope go in the same bag?',
          'a' => 'Most climbers keep the main line in a separate rope bag to protect it.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/notch-equipment/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/case-bag-1.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/case-bag-1-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'STE-NL-WK3-2-duffel-bag-10454',
        'creator' => 'Trendhim',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/148219711@N08',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/148219711@N08/50325892901',
      ),
    ),
    '/gear-bags/petzl-transport-45l-gear-pack/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/gear-bags/petzl-transport-45l-gear-pack/',
      'category' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/gear-storage/gear-bags/',
      'name' => 'Petzl Transport 45L Gear Pack',
      'brand' => 'petzl',
      'brand_name' => 'Petzl',
      'kind' => 'case-bag',
      'price' => 119,
      'keyword' => 'petzl transport 45l',
      'title' => 'Petzl Transport 45L Gear Pack for Rope Work',
      'h1' => 'Petzl Transport 45L Gear Pack',
      'meta' => 'The Petzl Transport 45L is a rugged gear pack for hauling climbing and rope access kit. See what it holds, why arborists use it, and how to care for it.',
      'tagline' => 'Petzl\'s 45-liter haul pack for climbing and rope work gear.',
      'summary' => 'The Petzl Transport 45L is a rugged gear pack built for carrying climbing and rope work equipment to the job. Arborists use it to keep a saddle, hardware, and lines together and protected between the truck and the tree.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => '45-liter gear pack from Petzl',
        1 => 'Tough fabric for job-site use',
        2 => 'Backpack carry to remote trees',
        3 => 'Keeps kit separated from saws and fluids',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Petzl',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Capacity',
          1 => '45 L',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Gear pack',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Built to be carried',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'When the tree is at the back of a property or down a slope, a pack with shoulder straps beats arm-carrying a bag. The Transport is a haul-style pack meant to take abuse, so it suits climbers who move their kit a long way on foot.',
            1 => 'Pack heavy hardware low and close to your back, and keep the saddle on top for quick setup at the tree.',
            2 => 'Carrying a pack instead of a bag also keeps your hands free for a saw, throw line, or rope bag. On long walks to a job, that alone can save a trip back to the truck. Adjust the shoulder straps before loading so the pack sits steady and does not swing as you walk.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Rinse off mud and sap, dry it open, and keep it away from fuel and bar oil in the truck. Inspect the gear you take out of it before every climb.',
            1 => 'Store the pack open and dry when you get back to the shop. Damp gear that sits zipped up can develop mildew, and fabric soft goods may need to be retired if they stay wet too long.',
            2 => 'See other <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/gear-storage/gear-bags/">gear bags</a>. Life-support gear must meet the applicable standard (ANSI Z133 and the manufacturer\'s instructions), be inspected before every use, and be used only by trained climbers.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can the Transport 45L carry a climbing rope?',
          'a' => 'Some ropes will fit along with other kit, depending on length. Many climbers still use a separate rope bag.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is it waterproof?',
          'a' => 'Check Petzl\'s product information for the fabric and closure details. Dry your gear after wet days either way.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/petzl/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/case-bag-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/case-bag-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'REL-NL-WK7-2-duffel-bag-10454',
        'creator' => 'Trendhim',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/148219711@N08',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/148219711@N08/50326073447',
      ),
