          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => '.404 chain is the heavy end of the range. It is run on big saws for felling large trees, bucking trunk wood and milling. The thick .063 gauge suits bars made for the largest saws. Chisel-style cutters cut fast in clean wood, while semi-chisel holds an edge longer in dirty or frozen wood, so check the cutter style before ordering for your conditions.',
            1 => 'Match the drive link count to your bar length, and confirm your bar is .063 gauge.',
            2 => 'Heavy chain also means more weight and more drag in the cut, so it pays to keep it sharp and well oiled. Running a dull .404 chain on a big saw makes the saw work far harder than it needs to, wastes fuel, and wears the bar and sprocket. Keep at least one spare loop per saw so you can swap and sharpen at lunch.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Sharpening and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Use the round file size Husqvarna specifies for this chain and a matching depth gauge tool. Keep every cutter the same length so the chain runs straight. Replace the drive sprocket when it shows wear, and keep the bar oiled. Large saws demand trained operators wearing chaps or saw pants, boots, helmet, eye and hearing protection.',
            1 => 'See more loops and reels in our <a href="/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chainsaw-bars-and-chain/chainsaw-chain/">chainsaw chain</a> section.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will .404 chain fit a 3/8 bar?',
          'a' => 'No. Pitch and gauge must match the bar and drive sprocket.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I know how many drive links I need?',
          'a' => 'Count the links on your old chain or read the stamp on the bar, which lists pitch, gauge and drive link count.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'felling',
        1 => 'ground',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/chain-bar-0.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/chain-bar-0-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Cutting Edge',
        'creator' => 'Clint__Budd',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/58827557@N06',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/58827557@N06/49188576927',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chainsaw-cases-and-scabbards/husqvarna-replacement-chainsaw-bar-scabbard/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chainsaw-cases-and-scabbards/husqvarna-replacement-chainsaw-bar-scabbard/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chainsaw-cases-and-scabbards/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Replacement Chainsaw Bar Scabbard',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'case-bag',
      'price' => 15,
      'keyword' => 'chainsaw bar scabbard',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna Replacement Chainsaw Bar Scabbard',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Replacement Chainsaw Bar Scabbard',
      'meta' => 'A Husqvarna chainsaw bar scabbard covers the chain for transport and storage. Protects your hands, the truck and the cutters. Pick the size for your bar.',
      'tagline' => 'Bar cover that protects the chain, your hands and the truck in transport.',
      'summary' => 'A Husqvarna chainsaw bar scabbard slips over the bar and chain whenever the saw is not running. It protects your hands and the truck bed, and keeps the cutters from being dulled by rocks and tools.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Covers bar and chain in transport',
        1 => 'Protects hands when carrying the saw',
        2 => 'Keeps cutters sharp in the truck',
        3 => 'Replacement for lost or cracked covers',
        4 => 'Choose the length that matches your bar',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Use',
          1 => 'Bar and chain cover',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Husqvarna',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fit',
          1 => 'Sized by bar length',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Cheap insurance',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Scabbards go missing on every crew. They get left on stumps, run over, or tossed in the brush pile. Running without one means a sharp chain banging against tools in the truck bed and a saw you have to carry carefully every time. A fresh scabbard keeps your chain sharp and your legs safe when you walk the saw to the next cut.',
            1 => 'Pick the size that covers your full bar length.',
            2 => 'Replacement scabbards are also worth having when you move to a new bar length, since an old short cover leaves the nose exposed. Many crews color mark their scabbards to match the saws so the right cover goes back on the right bar when the day ends.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Using it well',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Put the scabbard on whenever the saw is off and being moved or stored. Check that it clips or holds firmly on the bar. Keep a spare in the truck, since that is cheaper than a ruined chain. Saw operators should be trained and wear chaps or saw pants, eye, ear and head protection.',
            1 => 'Replace a scabbard that is cracked or no longer grips the bar, since one that slides off is worse than useless.',
            2 => 'More cases and covers are in our <a href="/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chainsaw-cases-and-scabbards/">chainsaw cases and scabbards</a> section.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Which size do I need?',
          'a' => 'Choose a scabbard that covers the full length of your bar. Check the listed bar lengths for each size.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will a Husqvarna scabbard fit other brands?',
          'a' => 'Often yes if the bar length matches, but fit at the powerhead end can vary.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
        1 => 'ground',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/case-bag-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/case-bag-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'REL-NL-WK7-2-duffel-bag-10454',
        'creator' => 'Trendhim',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/148219711@N08',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/148219711@N08/50326073447',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chaps-and-protective-gear/chainsaw-pants/arbortec-black-breatheflex-pro-chainsaw-pants/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chaps-and-protective-gear/chainsaw-pants/arbortec-black-breatheflex-pro-chainsaw-pants/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chaps-and-protective-gear/chainsaw-pants/',
      'name' => 'Arbortec BreatheFlex Pro Chainsaw Pants, Black',
      'brand' => 'arbortec',
      'brand_name' => 'Arbortec',
      'kind' => 'chaps-pants',
      'price' => 329,
      'keyword' => 'arbortec breatheflex pro chainsaw pants',
      'title' => 'Arbortec BreatheFlex Pro Chainsaw Pants, Black',
      'h1' => 'Arbortec BreatheFlex Pro Chainsaw Pants, Black',
      'meta' => 'Arbortec BreatheFlex Pro chainsaw pants in black: light, stretchy saw protection that breathes, for climbers and ground crews. Check the protection label.',
      'tagline' => 'Light, breathable stretch chainsaw pants for climbers and ground workers.',
      'summary' => 'Arbortec BreatheFlex Pro chainsaw pants put saw protection into a light, stretchy, breathable trouser, here in black. They are built for climbers and ground crews who want to move freely while still wearing leg protection.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Built-in chainsaw protection',
        1 => 'Stretch panels for climbing and kneeling',
        2 => 'Breathable fabric for warm days',
        3 => 'Black colorway',
        4 => 'Made by Arbortec for tree work',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Chainsaw protective pants',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Color',
          1 => 'Black',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Arbortec',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why climbers like saw pants',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Chaps work, but they flap, catch on limbs and get hot. Saw pants build the protective layers into the trouser, so nothing hangs loose when you are climbing, kneeling to buck, or dragging brush. The BreatheFlex Pro adds stretch and ventilation, which matter when you spend all day stepping up limbs or working through summer heat.',
            1 => 'Check the label for the protection class and rating, and buy the size that lets the protective panel cover the front of the legs when you crouch.',
            2 => 'BreatheFlex Pro pants are a popular choice for climbers who want saw protection without bulk. They also cut down on the snag points that chaps add when you are moving through a crown. Pick the color your crew prefers or your company requires.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Protection and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Saw protection works by fibers that pull out and clog the chain, so any cut through the outer layer means the pants are done in that area. Wash them as Arbortec instructs, since the wrong detergent or heat can reduce protection. Saw pants are not a substitute for training, good technique and the other PPE ANSI Z133 calls for.',
            1 => 'Hang saw pants to dry after wet days, and inspect them each morning for cuts, tears and worn knees before putting them on.',
            2 => 'Compare styles and colors in our <a href="/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chaps-and-protective-gear/chainsaw-pants/">chainsaw pants</a> section.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Are chainsaw pants better than chaps?',
          'a' => 'They protect the same way but fit closer, so they suit climbers and anyone who works in tight spots. Chaps are cheaper and easier to put on over other clothes.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can cut saw pants be repaired?',
          'a' => 'No. Once the protective layer is cut, replace the pants. A patch does not restore protection.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'apparel',
        1 => 'safety',
        2 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/arbortec/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/chaps-pants-0.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/chaps-pants-0-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Chainsaw Chaps',
        'creator' => 'photofarmer',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/62528187@N00',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/62528187@N00/8610687085',
      ),
    ),
