        2 => 'Restores idle and throttle response',
        3 => 'Works with the saw\'s AutoTune system',
        4 => 'Rule out fuel and air issues first',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna T540XP Mark II',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Carburetor assembly',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Saw type',
          1 => 'Gas top-handle',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Check the simple things first',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Most running problems on a top-handle saw are not the carburetor. Before replacing it, check for stale or wrongly mixed fuel, a clogged fuel filter, a dirty air filter, a fouled spark plug, a blocked spark arrestor screen, and cracked fuel lines. Old ethanol fuel left in a saw over the off-season is a common cause of varnished carbs.',
            1 => 'If the saw still will not hold an idle, bogs, or floods after those checks, a new carburetor assembly is often faster and more reliable than rebuilding a varnished one, especially on a climbing saw you depend on.',
            2 => 'Prevention is cheaper than a new carb. Use fresh, correctly mixed fuel, consider an ethanol-free or pre-mixed fuel for saws that sit, and run the tank dry before long storage.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Installing it',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The T540XP Mark II uses AutoTune, so follow Husqvarna\'s procedure for fitting the carb and letting the system relearn; a dealer can also check it with Husqvarna\'s service tools. Reconnect the fuel line and throttle linkage carefully, and confirm the chain does not turn at idle before using the saw.',
            1 => 'Shut the saw off and let it cool before servicing. A saw that runs badly aloft is a safety problem, so test it on the ground first. More parts are in <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">chainsaw parts</a>.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does the T540XP Mark II carburetor need adjusting?',
          'a' => 'The saw uses AutoTune, which adjusts the mixture automatically. Follow Husqvarna\'s instructions after installing a new carb.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What causes carburetor problems?',
          'a' => 'Stale or ethanol-heavy fuel, dirt past the filters, and long storage with fuel in the saw are the usual causes.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
        1 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
