          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Anti-vibration element assembly',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Husqvarna',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Saw displacement',
          1 => '50.1 cc',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'When AV elements wear out',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The 550XP Mark II is a common crew saw for limbing and bucking, and it spends a lot of hours running. Anti-vibration elements fatigue, and a broken one changes how the saw feels. You might notice the rear handle sagging, the saw twisting in your grip or a new rattle.',
            1 => 'Worn AV mounts make you work harder to control the saw and raise vibration exposure, which over time is hard on hands and arms.',
            2 => 'A simple check is to hold the saw by the rear handle and front handle with the engine off and gently twist. A little give is normal, since the system is designed to flex. A clunk, a sagging handle or a lot of free play points to a broken element. Checking AV mounts during regular service helps keep a crew saw comfortable and in control on long days.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Replacing it',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Check the parts diagram to see which location this assembly goes in. Remove the covers or handle needed for access, take out the old element and install the new one so it seats fully. Tighten fasteners to spec.',
            1 => 'Inspect every AV element while the saw is apart and replace any that look tired. More 550XP Mark II parts are in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">chainsaw parts</a> section.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will this fit the original 550XP?',
          'a' => 'Check the parts listing for your model. The Mark II has its own parts list.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I know an AV element is broken?',
          'a' => 'A loose or sagging handle, extra vibration and visible cracks or a separated spring or rubber are common signs.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/parts-0.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/parts-0-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'chainsaw',
        'creator' => 'sf-dvs',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/46207792@N00',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
