        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/46207792@N00/64064283',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-recoil-starter-handle/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-recoil-starter-handle/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Recoil Starter Handle',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'parts',
      'price' => 7,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna starter handle',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna Starter Handle: Recoil Pull Grip Replacement',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Recoil Starter Handle',
      'meta' => 'Replacement Husqvarna starter handle for recoil starters on chainsaws and other gear. Swap a cracked or lost pull grip when you replace starter rope.',
      'tagline' => 'A new pull grip for Husqvarna recoil starters. Cheap, and you\'ll want a spare.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna starter handle is the pull grip on the end of the starter rope on Husqvarna recoil starters. Handles crack from being dropped and slammed back, and once one breaks the rope can whip back into the housing and leave you with a saw you can\'t start.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Replacement recoil starter handle',
        1 => 'Fits a range of Husqvarna recoil starters, check your model',
        2 => 'Good time to swap it is with new starter rope',
        3 => 'Keep a spare in the saw kit',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Starter handle (pull grip)',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna recoil starters, check model',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Sold as',
          1 => 'Single handle',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why handles break',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'On the job, saws get started on the ground, on a stump, off a tailgate and in cold weather. Letting the rope snap back, or a hard drop on the handle side, eventually cracks the grip. A broken handle can also chew through the rope where it exits.',
            1 => 'If the handle is cracked, sharp or spinning loose, swap it before it fails in the field.',
            2 => 'A good handle also makes starting easier and safer. A cracked handle can pinch your glove or snap mid-pull, and a worn handle with a loose knot can let go and send the rope into the housing. On saws you start often, such as climbing saws and ground saws used for limbing and bucking, a new handle every season or two is reasonable. They are inexpensive, so keep one in the saw kit with a spare length of rope.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting a new handle',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Pull the rope out, hold tension on the recoil so it doesn\'t retract, and feed the rope through the new handle. Tie a firm knot and seat it in the handle pocket. Check the rope too. If it is frayed, replace it at the same time.',
            1 => 'Always let the rope rewind under control rather than letting go. More starter parts, including ropes, pulleys and springs, are in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">Husqvarna parts</a> section.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will this handle fit my Husqvarna saw?',
          'a' => 'It fits many Husqvarna recoil starters, but handle styles vary, so check your model before ordering.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Should I replace the starter rope too?',
          'a' => 'If the rope is frayed or glazed, yes. Doing both at once saves a second job.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
        1 => 'ground',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/parts-1.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/parts-1-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Route Clearance',
        'creator' => 'Georgia National Guard',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/40994485@N04',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/40994485@N04/33581236171',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-replaceable-nose-for-powermatch-bars/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-replaceable-nose-for-powermatch-bars/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Replaceable Nose for PowerMatch Bars',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'chain-bar',
      'price' => 30,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna replaceable bar nose',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna Replaceable Bar Nose for PowerMatch Bars',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Replaceable Nose for PowerMatch Bars',
      'meta' => 'Husqvarna replaceable bar nose for PowerMatch guide bars. Swap a worn or seized sprocket nose and keep a good bar body in service for longer bucking work.',
      'tagline' => 'Replacement sprocket nose that puts a worn PowerMatch bar back to work.',
      'summary' => 'The Husqvarna replaceable bar nose fits Husqvarna PowerMatch guide bars, letting you replace a worn or seized sprocket nose without buying a whole new bar. On longer pro bars, the nose usually wears out before the rails, so this is the cheap way to get more life from a good bar.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Replacement sprocket nose for PowerMatch-style bars',
        1 => 'Keeps a straight bar body in service',
        2 => 'Fixes a seized, chipped or worn nose sprocket',
        3 => 'Cheaper than a full bar on long pro lengths',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Replaceable sprocket nose',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna PowerMatch guide bars, match pitch and gauge',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Sold as',
          1 => 'Single nose',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'When to replace the nose',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The nose sprocket takes the hardest wear on a bar, especially on a saw that does a lot of bore cuts, felling and dirty bucking. Signs it is done: the sprocket won\'t spin freely, teeth are worn or chipped, there is side play, or the nose gets hot fast. A seized nose will wreck chain quickly.',
            1 => 'If the rails are still square and the bar is straight, a new nose is the right call.',
            2 => 'PowerMatch is a Husqvarna name used on some pro bars and drive systems, and nose types differ by bar series, pitch and gauge. Before ordering, check the markings on your bar and match the nose to it. A wrong nose will not fit the rivet pattern or will not run the chain properly. If your bar does not have a replaceable nose, this part will not fit, and a new bar is the answer.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting tips',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Replaceable noses are riveted on. Drill or grind out the old rivets, fit the new nose, and peen new rivets so the nose sits flush with the rails. Match the pitch and gauge of your bar and chain exactly. If you don\'t have the tools or the patience, a saw shop can do it quickly.',
            1 => 'Dress the rails and check chain fit after the swap. More bar and saw parts are in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">chainsaw parts</a> category.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I put this nose on any bar?',
          'a' => 'No. It is made for bars designed for a replaceable nose. Match the bar type, pitch and gauge.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I know the nose is worn out?',
          'a' => 'A sprocket that binds, has worn or chipped teeth, or wobbles side to side should be replaced.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
        1 => 'ground',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/chain-bar-1.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/chain-bar-1-sm.webp',
        'title' => '2021/365/233 New Tools Are Fun',
        'creator' => 'cogdogblog',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/37996646802@N01',
        'license' => 'CC0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/37996646802@N01/51432183709',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-replacement-nose-for-3-8-chainsaw-bars/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-replacement-nose-for-3-8-chainsaw-bars/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Replacement Nose for 3/8 Chainsaw Bars',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'chain-bar',
      'price' => 25,
      'keyword' => 'replacement nose for 3/8 chainsaw bar',
      'title' => 'Replacement Nose for 3/8 Chainsaw Bars by Husqvarna',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Replacement Nose for 3/8 Chainsaw Bars',
      'meta' => 'Husqvarna replacement nose for 3/8 chainsaw bars with a replaceable sprocket nose. Bring a worn bar back into service for felling and bucking work.',
      'tagline' => 'A 3/8-pitch sprocket nose for Husqvarna bars built to take a replaceable nose.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna replacement nose for 3/8 chainsaw bars swaps out a worn sprocket nose on bars made with a replaceable nose. When the rails are still good but the nose is tired, binding or chipped, fitting a new nose keeps a straight bar working for a fraction of the price of a new one.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Replacement sprocket nose for 3/8 inch pitch bars',
        1 => 'For bars designed with a replaceable nose',
        2 => 'Restores free-spinning nose sprocket',
        3 => 'Extends the life of long bars on bigger saws',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Replaceable sprocket nose',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Pitch',
          1 => '3/8 in',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna replaceable-nose bars, match gauge',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Sold as',
          1 => 'Single nose',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why replace just the nose',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => '3/8 pitch bars run on mid and large saws used for felling, bucking and storm cleanup. On those saws the nose sprocket wears first, especially if you bore cut a lot or run a dull chain. A bar with good rails and a dead nose is still worth saving.',
            1 => 'Look for a sprocket that won\'t spin freely, has chipped teeth or rocks side to side. Any of those means it\'s time.',
            2 => 'Long 3/8 pitch bars are expensive, so getting more life out of them makes sense for crews running big saws. Keep the nose greased, flip the bar regularly so the rails wear evenly, and keep the chain sharp so you are not forcing the bar through the cut. When the nose is finally worn out, replacing it is the cheapest way to keep a good bar in the rotation for another season.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting the nose',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Grind or drill out the old rivets, fit the new nose with matching gauge, and set new rivets so they sit flush. The nose must be centered with the rails or the chain will ride rough. If you\'d rather not peen rivets, a saw shop does this job routinely.',
            1 => 'Grease the nose sprocket through the bar\'s grease hole regularly once it\'s in service. See more bar parts in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">chainsaw parts</a> section.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does this fit .404 pitch bars?',
          'a' => 'No. This nose is for 3/8 inch pitch bars. Match pitch and gauge to your bar and chain.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Do I need special tools?',
          'a' => 'You need a way to remove the old rivets and peen new ones. Many people have a saw shop do it.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
        1 => 'ground',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/chain-bar-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/chain-bar-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => '20160823-FS-LSC-0474',
        'creator' => 'USDAgov',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/41284017@N08',
        'license' => 'Public domain',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/41284017@N08/28725898983',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-screw-fits-t540ixp-clutch/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-screw-fits-t540ixp-clutch/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Screw for T540iXP Clutch Side',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'parts',
      'price' => 4,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna t540ixp screw',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna T540iXP Screw for the Clutch Side',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Screw for T540iXP Clutch Side',
      'meta' => 'Replacement Husqvarna T540iXP screw for the clutch side of the battery top-handle saw. Replace a stripped or lost screw so covers and parts stay tight.',
      'tagline' => 'A replacement screw for the drive side of the T540iXP battery top-handle.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna T540iXP screw fits the clutch side (drive side) of the battery top-handle saw, the side where the sprocket, bar and chain run. Lost or stripped screws on a climbing saw are a small problem that can turn into a loose cover or rattling part, so replace them with the right one rather than whatever is in the truck.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Correct replacement screw for the T540iXP clutch side',
        1 => 'Replaces stripped, lost or damaged screws',
        2 => 'Right length and thread for the saw',
        3 => 'Small part, keeps a climbing saw tight',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Screw',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna T540iXP, clutch (drive) side',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Sold as',
          1 => 'Single screw',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why the right screw matters',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Husqvarna parts diagrams still call the chain side of the T540iXP the clutch side, even though it is a battery saw. Screws on that side hold parts that take vibration and chain loads all day. A screw that is too long can bottom out or hit internal parts, and one too short can strip the housing.',
            1 => 'Check the parts diagram for your saw to confirm the screw position before ordering.',
            2 => 'On a battery top-handle saw used daily, it pays to check screws on a regular schedule. Vibration, heat from cutting and being hung off a saddle loosen fasteners over time. A missing screw on the bar side can lead to a loose cover or brake part, which affects how the saw handles in the tree. Keep a couple of spare screws in the climbing kit so you can fix it on the spot.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting tips',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Remove the battery first. Clean the threads, start the screw by hand, and tighten it snug without overdoing it, since many threads on a top-handle saw are in plastic or light alloy. A dab of thread locker is sometimes specified, so follow the service manual.',
            1 => 'Top-handle saws are for trained arborists. Check the chain brake and that everything is tight before you climb. More T540iXP parts are in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">chainsaw parts</a> category.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Why is it called the clutch side on a battery saw?',
          'a' => 'Husqvarna\'s parts lists use the same side names across saws. On the T540iXP it means the bar and chain side.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I use a hardware-store screw instead?',
          'a' => 'It is better to use the correct part. Length, thread and head type matter in a small housing.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
        1 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/parts-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/parts-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Skoda Fabia Inlet Manifold',
        'creator' => 'L.C.Nøttaasen',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/35166455@N00',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/35166455@N00/4717400798',
      ),
