        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Tooth pocket',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'What the pocket does',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The pocket clamps the tooth to the cutter wheel and supports it against impact. When a pocket wears, cracks, or gets peened by rocks, the tooth no longer seats tightly. You will see teeth working loose, uneven cutting, and more vibration.',
            1 => 'Check pockets at every tooth change, especially after hitting rock or buried metal.',
            2 => 'Pockets can also wear on the face where the tooth seats. Even if the pocket looks whole, a tooth that will not tighten down square is a sign the pocket is done.',
            3 => 'Rocky sites, buried concrete, and old fence posts are hard on pockets. Probing around a stump and raking back loose stones before grinding helps protect both pockets and teeth.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting tips',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Lock out the grinder and clean the wheel. Fit the pocket in the correct orientation for the wheel\'s rotation, use good bolts and nuts, and torque to spec. Recheck after a short run.',
            1 => 'Change pockets in pairs or sets where your wheel layout calls for it, so the wheel stays balanced. Keep a spare pocket, bolts, and teeth in the grinder truck. A wheel that runs smooth and true cuts faster and is easier on bearings, belts, and the operator.',
            2 => 'Wear eye and face protection when grinding. Find teeth, bolts, and more <a href="/jobsite/stump-grinding/">stump grinding parts</a> in this section.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Do I need to replace pockets with teeth?',
          'a' => 'Not every time, but replace any pocket that is cracked, worn, or no longer holds a tooth tight.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will this fit my wheel?',
          'a' => 'It fits wheels set up for standard teeth. Compare it with your current pockets before ordering.',
        ),
      ),
