        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Keeping a rope puller in service',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A Maasdam rope puller is a simple hand-operated tool for pulling a tree over, freeing a hung top or tensioning a line, and like any tool that grips rope under load, its working parts wear. When the puller starts to slip or the action feels rough, swapping in fresh parts is usually all it needs.',
            1 => 'Check your puller\'s model and the kit contents before ordering so the parts match. You will find other pulling and <a href="/rigging/mechanical-advantage/">mechanical advantage</a> gear in the same section.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting and use',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Follow Maasdam\'s instructions for replacing parts, and test the puller under a light load before you trust it on a real pull. Use rope of the size and type the puller was designed for, because the wrong rope will slip or wear the grip quickly.',
            1 => 'Rope pullers can build a lot of force. Anchor to something sound, keep people out of the line of pull and well back from the tree, and stop if anything shifts. Rigging gear is for moving wood, not for life support. Match every component to the load with a working margin, follow the manufacturer\'s ratings and ANSI Z133, and make sure the crew is trained in rigging before relying on it. Note when each piece went into service, so worn gear gets retired on time instead of living on the truck for years.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I know my puller needs the kit?',
          'a' => 'If the puller slips under load, the action feels rough, or parts are visibly worn or damaged, it is time to service it or take it out of use.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will this fit every Maasdam puller?',
          'a' => 'Not necessarily. Confirm your model against the kit before ordering.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'rigging',
        1 => 'maintenance',
        2 => 'ground',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => NULL,
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/parts-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/parts-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Skoda Fabia Inlet Manifold',
        'creator' => 'L.C.Nøttaasen',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/35166455@N00',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/35166455@N00/4717400798',
      ),
    ),
    '/rigging/mechanical-advantage/petzl-jag-double-pulley/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/rigging/mechanical-advantage/petzl-jag-double-pulley/',
      'category' => '/rigging/mechanical-advantage/',
      'name' => 'Petzl JAG Double Pulley',
      'brand' => 'petzl',
      'brand_name' => 'Petzl',
      'kind' => 'pulley',
      'price' => 75,
      'keyword' => 'petzl jag',
      'title' => 'Petzl JAG Double Pulley for Haul Systems',
      'h1' => 'Petzl JAG Double Pulley',
      'meta' => 'The Petzl JAG is a compact double pulley with a becket, made for building haul and mechanical advantage systems. A light pulley for arborist pulls and rigging.',
      'tagline' => 'A compact double pulley with becket for building light haul systems.',
      'summary' => 'The Petzl JAG is a double pulley with a becket attachment point, built for setting up compact mechanical advantage systems. Arborists use it for tensioning lines, small pulls and haul setups where a big fiddle block would be overkill.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Two sheaves side by side plus a becket',
        1 => 'Compact and light for the saddle or bag',
        2 => 'Builds simple mechanical advantage systems',
        3 => 'Pairs with a second pulley for a basic haul kit',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Petzl',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Double pulley with becket',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Rope diameter',
          1 => '8 to 11 mm',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'How tree crews use it',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The JAG is small enough to live in a gear bag and quick to set up. Paired with another pulley and a length of rope, it makes a compact system for tensioning a speedline, snugging a guy line, or putting a controlled pull on a small leader before a cut.',
            1 => 'The becket gives you a place to tie off the rope end or attach a second pulley, which is how you build more advantage from a small kit. Compare it with heavier blocks in our <a href="/rigging/mechanical-advantage/">mechanical advantage</a> range.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Limits and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The JAG is a small pulley. It is not a substitute for a rigging block when you are catching and lowering wood, because the dynamic forces in rigging are far higher than a steady pull. Use it for controlled hauling and tensioning within Petzl\'s ratings.',
            1 => 'Check the sheaves turn freely and the side plates are not cracked or bent, and keep it clean of sap and grit. Rigging gear is for moving wood, not for life support. Match every component to the load with a working margin, follow the manufacturer\'s ratings and ANSI Z133, and make sure the crew is trained in rigging before relying on it. Note when each piece went into service, so worn gear gets retired on time instead of living on the truck for years.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What is the becket for?',
          'a' => 'It is an attachment point on the pulley where you tie off the rope end or clip a second pulley to build a haul system.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I use the JAG as a rigging block?',
          'a' => 'No. It is meant for hauling and tensioning, not for catching dynamic loads when rigging wood down.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'rigging',
        1 => 'ground',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/petzl/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/pulley-4.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/pulley-4-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Pulley Block Equipment Rigging Edited 2020',
        'creator' => 'chimpwithcan',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/188454520@N02',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/188454520@N02/49920521488',
      ),
