          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Samson designs its HyperClimb lines for climbers who move between stationary rope systems and doubled-rope climbing. A firm, consistent cover helps mechanical devices and rope wrenches run smoothly, while still holding a friction hitch.',
            1 => 'Before you buy, check Samson\'s spec sheet for the exact diameter and strength, and confirm the line is on your SRS device\'s approved rope list. The cool colorway helps separate your climbing line from rigging rope on a busy job.',
            2 => 'Whatever line you choose, set it up the same way every time: a clean termination, a hitch or device you have tested on that rope, and a stopper knot in the tail. Consistency is what makes a rope feel predictable at height, and it makes problems easier to spot.',
          ),
