            1 => 'Climbing rope is life-support equipment. It must meet the applicable standard, ANSI Z133 and the manufacturer\'s instructions. Inspect it before every climb for cuts, glazing, sheath damage and soft or stiff spots, keep it away from saws, fuel and bar oil, and retire it when in doubt. Get trained before you climb.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I use Yale Prism Climbing Rope for SRS as well as MRS?',
          'a' => 'Many 24-strand lines work for both, but device compatibility is set by the device maker. Check that your SRS device is approved for this rope and its diameter before you climb on it.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What hitch cord works with Yale Prism Climbing Rope?',
          'a' => 'Hitch cord should be smaller in diameter than the climbing line and tested on it before use. Tie the hitch, load it on the ground, and make sure it grabs and releases the way you expect.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
