            1 => 'Keep both clear and tinted pairs on hand so crew members can match the lens to the light as it changes through the day. Cheap glasses also reduce the temptation to keep wearing a scratched pair. Store them in a case or a clean bag rather than loose on the dash, where they scratch and pick up sap. A scratched lens is cheap to replace, so replace it.',
            2 => 'Wear safety glasses for saw work, chipping, and climbing, and add a face screen for heavy chip and sawdust exposure. Follow ANSI Z133 for personal protective equipment.',
