        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'What the visor carrier does',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The carrier is the frame that holds the screen and pivots on the helmet. On the Zenith it lets you add a mesh screen for chainsaw and chipper work, or a clear one when you want to keep fine debris and spray off your face.',
            1 => 'If your current carrier is cracked or will not hold its position, replacing it is a simple way to get the helmet back to full use. It also lets you convert a bare Zenith into a saw helmet. Look through our <a href="/safety/eye-protection/">eye protection</a> section for screens and glasses to go with it.',
            2 => 'Ground crews on the Zenith often run a mesh screen most of the day and swap to clear for stump grinding, where fine debris is constant. Having a spare carrier set up with the second screen makes that swap quick, rather than fiddling with screens in the field.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Setup and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Confirm the carrier and screen are listed for your Zenith version before you buy, and install them following Kask\'s instructions. Do not drill or modify the shell.',
            1 => 'Clean the screen and carrier after sappy or dusty days and check the pivots for play. A mesh screen does not stop all fine dust, so pair it with safety glasses when cutting dry wood.',
            2 => 'Store the helmet with the visor raised so the screen does not get pressed against other gear in the truck.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does the carrier come with a screen?',
          'a' => 'Check the listing. Carriers are often sold separately from screens so you can choose mesh or clear.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will this fit a Super Plasma?',
          'a' => 'It is listed for the Zenith. Super Plasma helmets use their own visor adapter, so match parts to your helmet model.',
