          1 => 'Pfanner Protos integrated helmet',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Pfanner',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'When a clear visor beats mesh',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Mesh visors are the standard for saw work because they do not fog and you can see through them in any light. But mesh lets fine dust through, and on a stump grinder or chipper that dust is constant. A clear visor stops it, which is why many Protos owners keep both and swap as the job changes.',
            1 => 'Clear visors also make sense for spraying and for anyone tired of fine sawdust in their eyes. Pair it with safety glasses if your job calls for them. Browse more <a href="/safety/eye-protection/">eye protection</a> for mesh screens and glasses.',
            2 => 'A clear visor is also handy when cutting with the sun low, since mesh can create glare and shadows that make it harder to read the kerf.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting and keeping it clear',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Install the visor following Pfanner\'s instructions for your version of the Protos and check that it locks in the up and down positions.',
            1 => 'Wash it with water and a soft cloth; wiping off dry sawdust scratches clear plastic quickly. Replace it when scratches or cracks are in your line of sight.',
            2 => 'Keep the clear visor in a soft bag when it is not on the helmet. Loose in a gear bin, it picks up scratches fast, and a scratched clear lens is harder to see through than a worn mesh one. Some users mark the date on a strip of tape when they fit a new visor so they know how long it has been in service.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does a clear visor fog up?',
          'a' => 'It can in cold or humid weather, especially when you are working hard. Many users keep a mesh visor for saw work and swap to clear for chipping and grinding.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will this fit an older Protos?',
          'a' => 'Pfanner has updated the Protos over the years. Check your helmet version against the listing before ordering.',
        ),
