      'meta' => 'The Arbortec Breatheflex Pro camo jacket in orange Realtree gives climbers a stretchy work jacket that stands out in the canopy. Fit, care and how it is used.',
      'tagline' => 'Orange Realtree camo stretch work jacket that stands out in the canopy.',
      'summary' => 'The Arbortec Breatheflex Pro camo jacket in orange Realtree is a stretchy, breathable work jacket that is easier to spot in the canopy than darker colors. It is a good fit for climbers who want freedom of movement and want the ground crew to see them.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Breatheflex Pro stretch fabric',
        1 => 'Orange Realtree camo pattern',
        2 => 'Easier for the ground crew to spot',
        3 => 'Breathable for hard work in cool weather',
        4 => 'Pairs with Breatheflex chainsaw pants',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Line',
          1 => 'Breatheflex Pro',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Pattern',
          1 => 'Realtree camo, orange',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Work jacket',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Arbortec',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why orange in the tree',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The ground crew needs to know where the climber is before they drop a piece, start the chipper or pull a line. A bright jacket helps, especially in leafy canopies and low light. The orange camo version gives you that visibility with a pattern that hides dirt better than solid color.',
            1 => 'The Breatheflex Pro fabric stretches, so it does not bind when you reach for a limb, and it lets heat out during hard climbs. See our <a href="/clothing/sweatshirts-and-jackets/">jackets and sweatshirts</a> for more.',
            2 => 'It makes sense off the tree as well. A groundie running the chipper or the rope is easier for the climber to see too, which helps when the climber is calling a piece down. Pair it with matching Breatheflex chainsaw pants for a kit that moves well.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fit and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Size it with room to layer underneath and so the sleeves and hem stay put when you reach overhead.',
            1 => 'Wash as the label directs. This jacket is not certified high-visibility apparel and is not chainsaw protection, so wear compliant high-vis near traffic and proper saw protection for cutting.',
            2 => 'Tuck or remove loose drawcords before climbing so they cannot snag on branches or catch in the saw.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is this a certified high-vis jacket?',
          'a' => 'Do not assume so. Check the label; for roadside work, wear apparel that meets the required high-visibility standard.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How does it compare to the brown version?',
          'a' => 'Same jacket and fabric, different color. Orange is easier to spot in the canopy.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'apparel',
        1 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/arbortec/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/apparel-3.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/apparel-3-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Great flannel shirts for women are hard to come by. But flannel is our signature, inspired by top-notch menswear shirts - especially designed and tailored for you. Take up to 20% off this weekend on all flannels, including the Park City flannel pictured h',
        'creator' => 'Tradlands',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/87743767@N07',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/87743767@N07/24785884538',
      ),
    ),
    '/shop-all/courant-phoenix-8mm-loop-prusik-with-aluminum-ring/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/shop-all/courant-phoenix-8mm-loop-prusik-with-aluminum-ring/',
      'category' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/hitch-cord-and-split-tails/',
      'name' => 'Courant Phoenix 8 mm Loop Prusik with Aluminum Ring',
      'brand' => 'courant',
      'brand_name' => 'Courant',
      'kind' => 'rope',
      'price' => 39,
      'keyword' => 'courant phoenix loop prusik',
      'title' => 'Courant Phoenix 8mm Loop Prusik with Ring',
      'h1' => 'Courant Phoenix 8 mm Loop Prusik with Aluminum Ring',
      'meta' => 'The Courant Phoenix loop prusik pairs 8mm hitch cord with an aluminum ring for a smooth-tending friction hitch. How it is used, fit to your rope and inspection.',
      'tagline' => 'Courant Phoenix 8 mm loop prusik with an aluminum ring for friction hitches.',
      'summary' => 'The Courant Phoenix loop prusik is a closed loop of 8 mm Phoenix hitch cord paired with an aluminum ring. The loop forms the friction hitch, and the ring gives a clean, smooth connection point to tend it.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Courant Phoenix 8 mm hitch cord',
        1 => 'Closed loop design',
        2 => 'Aluminum ring for a clean connection',
        3 => 'Used for friction hitches and adjusters',
        4 => 'Compact and easy to inspect',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Cord',
          1 => 'Courant Phoenix',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Diameter',
          1 => '8 mm',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Connector',
          1 => 'Aluminum ring',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Courant',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'How the loop and ring work',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A loop prusik is tied around the host rope to form a friction hitch, and the ring connects the hitch to your system. The ring gives a smooth surface for the cord to bear on and a tidy place to clip, which helps the hitch tend and release consistently.',
            1 => 'Courant\'s Phoenix cord is built for friction hitches. At 8 mm it suits many common climbing and lanyard ropes, but hitch behavior depends on the host rope, so test it before use. Our <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/hitch-cord-and-split-tails/">hitch cord and split tails</a> section has other options.',
            2 => 'Climbers use this setup on lanyards as an adjuster and on climbing systems as part of a hitch. The ring keeps the hitch clear of the carabiner gate and makes it easier to tend with a pulley, which helps the cord last longer.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Use and inspection',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Set the hitch low and test grip and release before committing. Watch for glazing, heat damage and wear where the cord meets the ring.',
            1 => 'Hitch cord in a climbing system is life-support equipment. Follow Courant\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, inspect it before every use, and retire it at the first sign of damage.',
            2 => 'Keep a spare loop in the gear bag; hitch cord wears faster than rope and swapping it takes minutes.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What is it used for?',
          'a' => 'Commonly as a friction hitch on a lanyard or climbing system, or as a rope grab. Check the manufacturer\'s approved uses.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will it grip my rope?',
          'a' => '8 mm cord grips many 11 to 13 mm ropes, but test it on your own rope close to the ground first.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/courant/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/rope-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/rope-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Coiling the Rope',
        'creator' => 'blachswan',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/40883175@N06',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/40883175@N06/34254142686',
      ),
    ),
    '/shop-all/endless-loop-round-slings-1/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/shop-all/endless-loop-round-slings-1/',
      'category' => '/rigging/rigging-slings/crane-slings/',
      'name' => 'Endless Loop Round Sling',
      'brand' => 'gap',
      'brand_name' => 'Gap Arborist Supply',
      'kind' => 'sling',
      'price' => 29,
      'keyword' => 'endless loop round sling',
      'title' => 'Endless Loop Round Sling for Crane and Rigging Work',
      'h1' => 'Endless Loop Round Sling',
      'meta' => 'An endless loop round sling for crane picks and heavy rigging on tree removals. How to choke or basket it, read the tag, and inspect it before every lift.',
      'tagline' => 'A soft, endless round sling for crane picks and heavy rigging points.',
      'summary' => 'An endless loop round sling is a continuous polyester sling with no eyes, so you can choke, basket, or hitch it straight around a stem. Crews use it for crane picks, heavy rigging points, and anywhere a soft sling is kinder to the bark than chain.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Endless loop, no eyes to wear out',
        1 => 'Soft on bark and on hardware',
        2 => 'Works in choker, basket, or vertical hitch',
        3 => 'Color and tag show the rated capacity',
        4 => 'Light to carry up the tree or hang on the boom',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Endless round sling',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Construction',
          1 => 'Load-bearing core yarns inside a protective cover',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Hitches',
          1 => 'Vertical, choker, basket',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Ratings',
          1 => 'Printed on the sling tag; varies by size',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Where a round sling fits on a tree job',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'On a crane removal the round sling is usually the first thing on the pick. Choke it around the stem above the cut, set the hook, and let the operator take the weight before the saw goes in. Because it has no eyes and no hardware, it wraps tight to the wood, lies flat, and is easy to free once the piece is on the ground.',
            1 => 'Round slings also earn their keep as heavy rigging points for a block, and as basket slings for lifting logs at the landing. Compared with wire rope or chain they are lighter, quieter, and far less likely to scar the trunk you are leaving behind. See the rest of our <a href="/rigging/rigging-slings/crane-slings/">crane slings</a> for other lengths and capacities.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Ratings, protection, and inspection',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Every round sling carries a tag with its rated capacity for each hitch. A choker hitch rates lower than a vertical pull, and a basket depends on the angle of the legs, so read the tag for the way you are actually rigging it. If the tag is missing or unreadable, the sling is out of service.',
            1 => 'The cover protects the core but it is not cut-proof. Keep the sling away from the saw, pad sharp edges, and never tie knots in it. Before each lift, look for cuts, burns, melted or stiff spots, exposed core yarns, and broken stitching. Crane work around trees should follow ANSI Z133, the sling maker\'s instructions, and a qualified operator and rigger.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I choke an endless round sling around a stem?',
          'a' => 'Yes. Choking is one of the most common ways to use it on a crane pick. Use the choker rating on the tag, which is lower than the vertical rating.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How long does a round sling last?',
          'a' => 'It depends on use and care. Retire it as soon as you find cuts, heat damage, exposed core yarns, or a missing tag.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'rigging',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/gap-arborist-supply/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/sling-3.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/sling-3-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Tree Pruning in RVA (Carytown, Virginia)',
        'creator' => 'Gamma Man',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/51625243@N06',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/51625243@N06/48982146938',
      ),
    ),
    '/shop-all/husqvarna-530ipt-battery-powered-pole-saw-without-batteries-or-charger/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/shop-all/husqvarna-530ipt-battery-powered-pole-saw-without-batteries-or-charger/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/battery-powered-equipment/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna 530iPT Battery Pole Saw (Tool Only)',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'pole-saw',
      'price' => 549,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna 530ipt',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna 530iPT Battery Pole Saw, Tool Only',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna 530iPT Battery Pole Saw (No Battery or Charger)',
      'meta' => 'The Husqvarna 530iPT telescoping battery pole saw, sold as a bare tool for crews already on Husqvarna 36V batteries. What it cuts, reach, and buying tips.',
      'tagline' => 'A telescoping 36V pole saw for ground pruning, sold without battery or charger.',
      'summary' => 'The Husqvarna 530iPT is a telescoping battery pole saw built for pruning and clearance work from the ground. This listing is the bare tool, aimed at crews that already run Husqvarna 36V batteries and chargers.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Telescoping shaft for adjustable reach',
        1 => 'Runs on Husqvarna 36V batteries',
        2 => 'Quiet, no fuel mix, no exhaust',
        3 => 'Good fit for lift clearance and street pruning',
        4 => 'Bare tool: battery and charger sold separately',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Power',
          1 => 'Husqvarna 36V battery system',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Shaft',
          1 => 'Telescoping',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Included',
          1 => 'Pole saw only; no battery or charger',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Bar length',
          1 => '10 in',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Where the 530iPT earns its place',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A battery pole saw shines on the jobs where a gas pole saw is overkill: raising canopies over sidewalks, clearing limbs off a roof line, and cleaning up after a climber without sending anyone back up. With no pull cord and no exhaust it starts on the trigger, runs quiet enough for residential streets, and does not stink up a client\'s patio.',
            1 => 'The telescoping shaft lets one tool cover low limbs and high ones. Keep cuts within the bar\'s capacity, undercut heavier limbs to stop bark tearing, and stand out from under the drop zone. Browse other <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/battery-powered-equipment/">battery-powered equipment</a> if you are building out a cordless kit.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Buying the bare tool',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Buying tool-only makes sense if you already own Husqvarna 36V batteries from a top-handle saw, blower, or trimmer. If you are new to the platform, price a battery and charger alongside it, since runtime depends on the battery you pair with it.',
            1 => 'Wear a helmet, eye protection, and gloves, keep the saw well clear of power lines, and only let trained workers operate it near energized conductors. Follow ANSI Z133 and the Husqvarna operator\'s manual for chain tension, lubrication, and maintenance.',
            2 => 'On a typical day it rides in the truck next to the climber\'s gear and comes out for the cleanup cuts nobody wants to climb for.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does the 530iPT come with a battery?',
          'a' => 'Not this version. It is sold as a bare tool, so you need a compatible Husqvarna 36V battery and charger.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I use a pole saw near power lines?',
          'a' => 'Only qualified line-clearance workers should work near energized lines. Everyone else must keep the required clearance distances under ANSI Z133.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'pruning',
        1 => 'ground',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/pole-saw-1.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/pole-saw-1-sm.webp',
        'title' => '2009. Lorraine MacLauchlan (B.C. Ministry of Forests, Southern Interior Region) with pole-pruner to sample Douglas-fir tussock moth larvae, pre-spray. Testing the effectiveness of low-dose application rates of TM-Biocontrol-1. Kamloops, B.C.',
        'creator' => 'USDA Forest Service',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/151887236@N05',
        'license' => 'Public domain',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/151887236@N05/39161789941',
      ),
    ),
    '/shop-all/husqvarna-fixed-pulley-pruner-with-adapter-and-rope/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/shop-all/husqvarna-fixed-pulley-pruner-with-adapter-and-rope/',
      'category' => '/cutting-and-pruning/poles-and-kits/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Fixed Pulley Pruner with Adapter and Rope',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'pruner',
      'price' => 89,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna fixed pulley pruner',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna Fixed Pulley Pruner with Adapter and Rope',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Fixed Pulley Pruner with Adapter and Rope',
      'meta' => 'A Husqvarna fixed pulley pruner head with adapter and pull rope for clean pole cuts on small limbs. Where it fits in a pole kit and how to keep it cutting.',
      'tagline' => 'A rope-pull bypass pruner head that mounts on a pole for clean cuts out of reach.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna fixed pulley pruner is a rope-operated pruner head that mounts to a pole with the included adapter. It makes clean, flush cuts on small limbs and suckers that are out of reach, without a saw.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Fixed pulley head for added cutting force',
        1 => 'Adapter for pole mounting included',
        2 => 'Pull rope included',
        3 => 'Clean cuts on small-diameter wood',
        4 => 'Pairs with a pole saw head on the same pole set',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Rope-operated pole pruner head',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Includes',
          1 => 'Pruner head, adapter, pull rope',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Mount',
          1 => 'Pole adapter (check fit with your pole system)',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'What a pulley pruner is good for',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A pole pruner does the small, fussy cuts a pole saw does poorly: water sprouts, suckers, deadwood twigs, and fine thinning cuts where you want a clean collar cut instead of a ragged saw kerf. The pulley in the head multiplies your pull on the rope, so the blade closes with more force than a straight lever would give you.',
            1 => 'Most crews carry a pruner head and a saw head for the same pole set and swap between them as the job changes. Check that the adapter matches your poles before you head out. You can find poles and complete setups in our <a href="/cutting-and-pruning/poles-and-kits/">poles and kits</a> section.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Keeping it sharp and safe',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Keep the blade sharp and the pivot clean and lightly oiled; a dull pruner crushes bark instead of cutting it. Check the pull rope for wear where it runs through the pulley and replace it before it frays through. Do not force the head on wood larger than it is built to cut, since that bends the blade and opens up the bypass gap.',
            1 => 'Wear eye protection and a helmet when cutting overhead. Never use a pole tool near energized power lines unless you are a qualified line-clearance worker following ANSI Z133.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does the pruner fit any pole?',
          'a' => 'It mounts with the included adapter. Confirm the adapter matches your pole system before buying.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How big a limb can it cut?',
          'a' => 'Pole pruners are meant for small limbs. Use a pole saw for anything thick enough that the pruner strains to close.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'pruning',
        1 => 'ground',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/pruner-0.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/pruner-0-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Pruning shears - apple orchard - winter DSC_8276',
        'creator' => 'Apple and Pear Australia Ltd',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/113312228@N06',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/113312228@N06/28115965045',
      ),
    ),
    '/shop-all/husqvarna-pole-saw-head-with-center-saw-blade-mount/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/shop-all/husqvarna-pole-saw-head-with-center-saw-blade-mount/',
      'category' => '/cutting-and-pruning/pole-saws-and-scabbards/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Pole Saw Head with Center Saw Blade Mount',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'pole-saw',
      'price' => 45,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna pole saw head',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna Pole Saw Head with Center Blade Mount',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Pole Saw Head with Center Saw Blade Mount',
      'meta' => 'A Husqvarna pole saw head with a center blade mount, so the blade lines up with the pole for straight pulls. How it fits a pole kit and what to check first.',
      'tagline' => 'A pole saw head that centers the blade on the pole for straighter cuts.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna pole saw head holds a pruning saw blade on a center mount, so the blade runs in line with the pole. That alignment makes pull strokes straighter and keeps the saw from twisting in the cut.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Center blade mount keeps the blade in line with the pole',
        1 => 'Fits a pole saw blade for overhead cutting',
        2 => 'Straighter strokes, less twisting',
        3 => 'Pairs with a pruner head on the same pole set',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Pole saw head',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Blade mount',
          1 => 'Center mount',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Blade',
          1 => 'Sold separately unless listed',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why a center mount matters',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'When the blade sits off to one side of the pole, every pull stroke tries to roll the saw over, and the cut wanders. A center mount puts the blade right on the pole\'s axis, so your pull goes straight into the kerf. On long reaches that difference is easy to feel in your shoulders by the end of the day.',
            1 => 'The head lets you swap blades as they wear and move between a saw and a pruner head on one set of poles. See the full range of <a href="/cutting-and-pruning/pole-saws-and-scabbards/">pole saws and scabbards</a> for blades and covers.',
            2 => 'A center mount also makes it easier to hook a hanger or stub and pull it free without the head twisting off line.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Setup and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Make sure the head and blade match your pole system and that the blade bolts are snug before every use; a loose blade chatters and can drop out of the cut. Clean sap off the blade and head at the end of the day and store the saw in a scabbard to protect the teeth and the crew.',
            1 => 'Cut from the side, not from directly under the limb, and keep a clear drop zone. Wear a helmet and eye protection, and stay clear of power lines unless you are qualified for line clearance under ANSI Z133.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does this include a saw blade?',
          'a' => 'It is listed as a saw head. Check the listing for whether a blade is included, and match any blade to the mount.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will it fit my poles?',
