          0 => 'Sold',
          1 => 'By the foot',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Sterling Rope',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Use',
          1 => 'Lanyards, fliplines, custom components',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why buy rope by the foot',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Off-the-shelf lanyards come in a few lengths. If you climb big spars, work in a bucket, or just like a specific length, buying rope by the foot lets you build exactly what you need and re-use your existing snap and adjuster.',
            1 => 'Measure your current lanyard, then add enough for terminations: a sewn eye, a spliced eye, or a stopper knot all take rope. Browse our <a href="/rope/tech-cordage/">tech cordage</a> section for hitch cord and other cut-to-length rope.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Terminations and inspection',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Any eye or termination used for life support must be made by a qualified person using a method the rope maker approves, or tied with a knot you have been trained on. A home-made splice in rope you are not familiar with is not a shortcut worth taking.',
            1 => 'Inspect the rope before each climb for cuts, glazing, and stiff or flat spots, and keep the saw well clear of any rope lanyard. Treat it as life-support equipment: it must meet ANSI Z133 and the manufacturer\'s instructions, be inspected before every climb, and be used only by trained climbers.',
            2 => 'Keep a record of when the lanyard was built and what went into it, so you know its age and can retire it on schedule.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How much should I order for a lanyard?',
          'a' => 'Measure the working length you want and add enough for your terminations. When in doubt, order a little extra.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I splice TriTech myself?',
          'a' => 'Only if you are trained in a splice the manufacturer approves for this rope. Otherwise have it spliced by a qualified splicer.',
        ),
      ),
