        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'When to replace the clutch drum',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The sprocket on the clutch drum drives the chain, and it wears every time the saw cuts. A worn sprocket has grooves where the chain drive links sit and will chew up a new chain quickly. Many saw shops suggest replacing the sprocket every two chains or so, or whenever you see clear wear.',
            1 => 'Also replace the drum if it is blued from heat, cracked, or wobbles on the crank, or if the needle bearing is worn.',
            2 => 'A worn clutch drum can also make the saw feel rough or noisy at idle, and a damaged needle bearing can let the drum wobble and wear the chain unevenly. If the chain keeps turning at idle, look at the clutch springs and idle setting too. Inspect the drum whenever you change the chain, so problems are caught before they damage other parts.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting the new drum',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Match the sprocket pitch to your bar and chain, and grease the needle bearing per Husqvarna\'s service information. Check the clutch shoes and springs while you are in there. More parts are in <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">power equipment parts</a>.',
            1 => 'Make sure the saw is off and cool before working on it, and test the chain brake after reassembly.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Do I need to change the chain at the same time?',
          'a' => 'Running a new chain on a worn sprocket shortens its life, and an old chain can wear a new sprocket fast. Many crews replace them together.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will this fit the original 550XP?',
          'a' => 'Confirm compatibility for your exact model and version before ordering.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/parts-1.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/parts-1-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Route Clearance',
        'creator' => 'Georgia National Guard',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/40994485@N04',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/40994485@N04/33581236171',
      ),
    ),
    '/climbing/climbing-gear/friction-savers/buckingham-treesqueeze/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/friction-savers/buckingham-treesqueeze/',
      'category' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/friction-savers/',
      'name' => 'Buckingham TreeSqueeze Friction Saver',
      'brand' => 'buckingham',
      'brand_name' => 'Buckingham',
      'kind' => 'friction-device',
      'price' => 89,
      'keyword' => 'buckingham treesqueeze',
      'title' => 'Buckingham TreeSqueeze Friction Saver',
      'h1' => 'Buckingham TreeSqueeze',
      'meta' => 'The Buckingham TreeSqueeze is a friction saver that protects the bark and your rope at the tie-in point. How it works, setup tips, inspection, and price.',
      'tagline' => 'A Buckingham friction saver for protecting the tree and your climbing line at the tie-in.',
      'summary' => 'The Buckingham TreeSqueeze is a friction saver from Buckingham, used at the tie-in point to protect the tree\'s bark and cut down wear on the climbing line. It gives a smoother, more predictable tie-in than running rope directly over a branch union.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Protects bark at the tie-in point',
        1 => 'Reduces wear on your climbing line',
        2 => 'Smoother, more predictable rope movement',
        3 => 'From Buckingham, a long-time arborist gear maker',
        4 => 'Retrievable from the ground with practice',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Buckingham',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Friction saver',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'System',
          1 => 'Moving rope (MRS/DdRT) tie-in',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why use a friction saver',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Running a climbing line straight over a union generates heat, wears the rope, and damages the cambium. A friction saver puts a protective sleeve or connectors at the crotch so the rope runs on hardware instead of bark. The tree stays healthier and your rope lasts longer, and rope movement is smoother and easier to predict.',
            1 => 'Set it high in a sound union with the rings or connectors positioned so they do not bind. Learn the retrieval method for your system on the ground before relying on it.',
            2 => 'Friction savers also make it easier to repeat climbs in the same tree. Once the saver is set, the climber can come down, move ground gear and go back up on the same tie-in without fighting rope friction over bark. On trees with thin or sensitive bark, the protection it gives the cambium is worth the small extra time spent on setup.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Inspection and safe use',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A friction saver is part of your life-support system. Inspect the sleeve, rope or webbing and hardware before each climb and retire it at the first sign of cuts, heavy wear or heat damage. Compare other <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/friction-savers/">friction savers</a> if you want an adjustable model.',
            1 => 'Life-support gear must meet the applicable standard, be used per the manufacturer\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, be inspected before every climb, and be used only by trained climbers.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I retrieve the TreeSqueeze from the ground?',
          'a' => 'Many friction savers can be retrieved from the ground with the right setup. Follow Buckingham\'s instructions and practice low before using it aloft.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is a friction saver required?',
          'a' => 'Not always, but it protects the tree and rope and is widely recommended for moving rope climbing.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/buckingham/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/friction-device-0.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/friction-device-0-sm.webp',
        'title' => '100127-F-9898L-026',
        'creator' => 'expertinfantry',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/58297778@N04',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/58297778@N04/5444263877',
      ),
    ),
    '/climbing/climbing-gear/fliplines-and-lanyards/lanyard-kits/teufelberger-hipstar-flex-light-lanyard/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/fliplines-and-lanyards/lanyard-kits/teufelberger-hipstar-flex-light-lanyard/',
      'category' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/fliplines-and-lanyards/lanyard-kits/',
      'name' => 'Teufelberger hipSTAR Flex Light Lanyard',
      'brand' => 'teufelberger',
      'brand_name' => 'Teufelberger',
      'kind' => 'lanyard',
      'price' => 179,
      'keyword' => 'teufelberger hipstar flex light',
      'title' => 'Teufelberger hipSTAR Flex Light Lanyard',
      'h1' => 'Teufelberger hipSTAR Flex Light Lanyard',
      'meta' => 'The Teufelberger hipSTAR Flex Light is a light, adjustable positioning lanyard for arborists who move around the tree. Setup notes, inspection, and price.',
      'tagline' => 'A lightweight adjustable lanyard kit from Teufelberger for everyday work positioning.',
      'summary' => 'The Teufelberger hipSTAR Flex Light lanyard is a lightweight adjustable positioning lanyard for climbers who want less weight on the saddle and quick length changes while working. It suits climbers who reposition often during pruning and removals.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Lightweight positioning lanyard from Teufelberger',
        1 => 'Adjustable length for quick repositioning',
        2 => 'Less weight on the saddle on long days',
        3 => 'Suited to pruning and removal work',
        4 => 'Inspect rope, adjuster and connectors every climb',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Teufelberger',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Adjustable positioning lanyard',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Use',
          1 => 'Work positioning',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why a lighter lanyard',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A lanyard rides on your saddle every minute you are in the tree, so weight adds up. A lighter lanyard is easier to throw around a stem and less tiring to carry on long climbs. The adjustable design lets you tighten up to lean back into a cut, then let out slack to move around the stem.',
            1 => 'Check what adjuster and connectors come in the kit, and make sure they suit your saddle setup and the way you clip in.',
            2 => 'Lighter lanyards also tend to be more comfortable on long pruning days, when the climber moves around the canopy far more than on a straightforward removal. Less weight hanging on the side D-rings means less drag on the saddle and less fatigue by late afternoon. Make sure the lanyard length and connectors still suit the largest stems you plan to work around.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Inspection and safe use',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Inspect the rope, terminations, adjuster and carabiners before every climb. A lanyard is not cut-resistant; keep the saw well clear and consider a steel-core flipline for heavy saw work. More options are in <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/fliplines-and-lanyards/lanyard-kits/">lanyard kits</a>.',
            1 => 'Life-support gear must meet the applicable standard, be used per the manufacturer\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, be inspected before every climb, and be used only by trained climbers.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is the hipSTAR Flex Light a primary climbing system?',
          'a' => 'No. It is a positioning lanyard used alongside your main climbing system.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How long should the lanyard be?',
          'a' => 'Choose a length that wraps the largest stems you typically work on with room to adjust. Longer lanyards are more versatile but carry more weight.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/teufelberger/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/lanyard-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/lanyard-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Arborist climbing on the tree',
        'creator' => 'Yuliya Krasylenko',
        'creator_url' => 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Yuliya_Krasylenko',
        'license' => 'CC BY 4.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=97167024',
      ),
    ),
    '/climbing/climbing-gear/carabiners-and-hardware/auto-locking-carabiners/dmm-american-o-ansi-gate-carabiner/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/carabiners-and-hardware/auto-locking-carabiners/dmm-american-o-ansi-gate-carabiner/',
      'category' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/carabiners-and-hardware/auto-locking-carabiners/',
      'name' => 'DMM American O ANSI Gate Carabiner',
      'brand' => 'dmm',
      'brand_name' => 'DMM',
      'kind' => 'carabiner',
      'price' => 28,
      'keyword' => 'dmm american o carabiner',
      'title' => 'DMM American O ANSI Gate Carabiner',
      'h1' => 'DMM American O ANSI Gate Carabiner',
      'meta' => 'The DMM American O ANSI gate carabiner is an oval auto-locking biner for pulleys, rings and climbing systems. Where an oval shines, what to check, and price.',
      'tagline' => 'An oval auto-locking DMM carabiner with a gate built for the US market.',
      'summary' => 'The DMM American O ANSI gate carabiner is an oval auto-locking carabiner made for climbers who need a high-strength gate in their system. Its symmetrical oval shape keeps pulleys, rings and devices centered under load.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Oval shape keeps hardware centered',
        1 => 'Auto-locking gate',
        2 => 'Gate made to suit US ANSI requirements, per DMM',
        3 => 'Good with micro pulleys and rings',
        4 => 'Check markings on the spine for ratings',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'DMM',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Shape',
          1 => 'Oval',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Gate',
          1 => 'Auto-locking',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why an oval',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Oval carabiners load evenly on both sides, which keeps a micro pulley, ring or device sitting square instead of sliding toward the narrow end as it would in a D. That makes ovals a natural pick for a hitch climber pulley, for clipping a rope wrench, or for anything that needs to stay aligned while it moves.',
            1 => 'The ANSI gate designation means DMM built the gate for the higher gate strength required in US standards. Read the ratings on the carabiner itself to confirm it meets the requirement for your use.',
            2 => 'Many climbers keep a couple of ovals in their kit specifically for pulleys and rings and use D-shaped biners for the lanyard and bridge, where strength along the spine matters most. Keeping the oval in that role makes it easy to check, and makes sure its strength rating is well suited to the job you are asking of it each day.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Inspection and use',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Check for rope grooves, sharp edges, cracks and a gate that sticks or does not lock on its own. Retire any carabiner dropped from height onto a hard surface. Compare other <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/carabiners-and-hardware/auto-locking-carabiners/">auto-locking carabiners</a> for D or offset shapes.',
            1 => 'Life-support gear must meet the applicable standard, be used per the manufacturer\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, be inspected before every climb, and be used only by trained climbers.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What does ANSI gate mean?',
          'a' => 'It indicates a gate built for the higher gate strength in US ANSI requirements. Confirm with the markings and DMM\'s instructions.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is an oval weaker than a D?',
          'a' => 'Ovals often have lower major-axis ratings than D shapes of similar size. Check the markings to make sure it suits your use.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/dmm/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/carabiner-3.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/carabiner-3-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'carabiner+chains',
        'creator' => 'brenkee',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/55128416@N05',
        'license' => 'CC0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/55128416@N05/12835828245',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chainsaw-bars-and-chain/chainsaw-bars/husqvarna-double-guard-chainsaw-bar-3-8-mini-pixel-x-050/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chainsaw-bars-and-chain/chainsaw-bars/husqvarna-double-guard-chainsaw-bar-3-8-mini-pixel-x-050/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chainsaw-bars-and-chain/chainsaw-bars/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Double Guard Chainsaw Bar, 3/8 in Mini Pixel, .050',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'chain-bar',
      'price' => 35,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna double guard bar',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna Double Guard Bar, 3/8 Mini Pixel .050',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Double Guard Chainsaw Bar, 3/8 in Mini Pixel, .050 in',
      'meta' => 'The Husqvarna Double Guard chainsaw bar runs 3/8 in mini Pixel chain at .050 gauge for small saws. Fit checks, chain matching, and the typical street price.',
      'tagline' => 'A small-saw bar from Husqvarna sized for 3/8 in mini Pixel chain.',
      'summary' => 'The Husqvarna Double Guard chainsaw bar is a replacement bar for small saws running 3/8 in mini Pixel chain in .050 gauge. It suits light-duty and top-handle saws used for pruning and small limb work.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Runs 3/8 in mini Pixel chain',
        1 => 'Gauge .050 in',
        2 => 'Replacement bar for small Husqvarna saws',
        3 => 'Light weight for pruning and limbing',
        4 => 'Confirm length and mount for your saw',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Pitch',
          1 => '3/8 in mini (Pixel)',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Gauge',
          1 => '.050 in',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Husqvarna',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Replacement chainsaw bar',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Matching bar, chain and saw',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A bar has to match three things: the saw\'s mount, the chain pitch and the gauge. This bar is set up for 3/8 in mini pitch chain, the narrow-kerf Pixel style Husqvarna uses on many small saws, at .050 in gauge. Check your saw\'s manual for approved bar lengths and mounts, and match the drive link count to the bar length.',
            1 => 'Small-kerf chain cuts fast with less power, which is why it suits compact and top-handle saws.',
            2 => 'Small saws with narrow-kerf chain are popular for pruning because they cut quickly and are light to carry aloft. That same narrow kerf means the bar and chain wear faster if they are not kept sharp and well oiled. Check that the oiler is working and keep spare chains on hand, so the bar is never run with a dull or dry chain.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Bar care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Flip the bar regularly so the rails wear evenly, clean out the groove and oil hole, and dress burrs off the rails with a file. Replace the bar if the rails are spread, the groove is worn shallow, or the nose is damaged. Other sizes are in <a href="/jobsite/chainsaw-accessories/chainsaw-bars-and-chain/chainsaw-bars/">chainsaw bars</a>.',
            1 => 'Keep the chain sharp and correctly tensioned and wear chainsaw protective gear, following the operator\'s manual and ANSI Z133.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will regular 3/8 in chain fit this bar?',
          'a' => 'No. This bar is for 3/8 in mini (low profile) chain, not full-size 3/8 in chain.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What length do I need?',
          'a' => 'Check your saw\'s manual for approved bar lengths and order the matching chain length and drive link count.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
        1 => 'pruning',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/chain-bar-1.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/chain-bar-1-sm.webp',
        'title' => '2021/365/233 New Tools Are Fun',
        'creator' => 'cogdogblog',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/37996646802@N01',
        'license' => 'CC0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/37996646802@N01/51432183709',
      ),
    ),
    '/rigging/rigging-kits/isc-1-2-rigging-block-with-loopie-sling/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/rigging/rigging-kits/isc-1-2-rigging-block-with-loopie-sling/',
      'category' => '/rigging/rigging-kits/',
      'name' => 'ISC 1/2 in Rigging Block with Loopie Sling',
      'brand' => 'isc',
      'brand_name' => 'ISC',
      'kind' => 'rigging-device',
      'price' => 199,
      'keyword' => 'isc rigging block with loopie sling',
      'title' => 'ISC 1/2 in Rigging Block with Loopie Sling',
      'h1' => 'ISC 1/2 in Rigging Block with Loopie Sling',
      'meta' => 'An ISC 1/2 in rigging block paired with a loopie sling for setting fast, adjustable rigging points on light to mid-size wood. How it rigs, checks, and price.',
      'tagline' => 'An ISC rigging block for 1/2 in rope, paired with an adjustable loopie sling.',
      'summary' => 'This ISC 1/2 in rigging block with loopie sling is a ready-to-go rigging kit for light to mid-size wood. The loopie cinches to the stem and the block gives you a clean, low-friction redirect for your lowering line.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'ISC rigging block for 1/2 in rope',
        1 => 'Adjustable loopie sling included',
        2 => 'Side plates open to load the rope mid-line',
        3 => 'For limb lowering and small tops',
        4 => 'Check ratings on the block and sling',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'ISC',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Rope size',
          1 => '1/2 in',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Sling',
          1 => 'Loopie (adjustable)',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Rigging block kit',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Setting a rigging point with block and loopie',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A block above the work lets you lower pieces with the rope running over a sheave instead of rubbing over bark. The loopie is an adjustable sling that cinches tight to the stem, so it fits a range of diameters and holds its place. Together they make a rigging point you can set in a minute and retrieve easily.',
            1 => 'A 1/2 in kit is aimed at limbs and small tops. For bigger pieces, move up to a larger block, rope and sling rated for the forces involved.',
            2 => 'Kits like this save time on the job because all the parts are matched and ready to go. The block and sling stay together in the bag, so the climber can grab one kit and know everything inside suits the same rope size. Keep a spare set of carabiners or shackles with it that match the block\'s rating, so nothing gets mixed up.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Ratings and inspection',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Check the working load limit and MBS on the block and sling, and match the rigging line and connectors. Rigging loads can be several times the piece\'s weight once it starts moving. Other kits are in <a href="/rigging/rigging-kits/">rigging kits</a>.',
            1 => 'Inspect the sheave, bearing, side plates and sling before each job. Rig within the rated strength of every component, inspect gear before each job, and make sure the crew is trained in rigging practice under ANSI Z133 and the manufacturer\'s instructions.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I use 5/8 in rope in this block?',
          'a' => 'Use only the rope sizes ISC lists for the block. This kit is sized for 1/2 in rope.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is the loopie adjustable?',
          'a' => 'Yes. A loopie cinches and adjusts to fit different stem sizes.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'rigging',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/isc/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/rigging-device-5.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/rigging-device-5-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Nautical #5',
        'creator' => 'Graham B Finney',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/188487900@N02',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/188487900@N02/51798984894',
