      'keyword' => 'yale ring lanyard kit',
      'title' => 'Yale R.I.N.G. Lanyard Kit with Triple Locking Snap',
      'h1' => 'Yale R.I.N.G. Lanyard Kit with Triple Locking Snap',
      'meta' => 'The Yale R.I.N.G. lanyard kit with a triple locking snap, for flipping and holding work position on the stem. What is in it, how to use it and inspect it.',
      'tagline' => 'Yale R.I.N.G. rope positioning lanyard kit terminated with a triple-locking snap.',
      'summary' => 'The Yale R.I.N.G. lanyard kit with a triple locking snap is a positioning lanyard built on Yale Cordage rope, terminated with a snap that clips cleanly to your saddle\'s side D-ring. It gives you an adjustable second attachment for spar work and positioning on limbs.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Yale Cordage R.I.N.G. rope',
        1 => 'Triple-locking snap termination',
        2 => 'Clips neatly into side D-rings',
        3 => 'Adjustable work-positioning lanyard',
        4 => 'Kit saves sourcing parts separately',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Rope',
          1 => 'Yale R.I.N.G.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Connector',
          1 => 'Triple-locking snap',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Positioning lanyard kit',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Yale Cordage',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Snap-terminated lanyards',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Many climbers prefer a snap on the lanyard end because it sits flat in a side D-ring and is quick to clip with a gloved hand. A triple-locking snap adds an extra deliberate step to open, which makes accidental opening against bark or rope much less likely.',
            1 => 'Yale Cordage is a long-time US rope maker for arborists and industry. If you prefer a carabiner-terminated version, compare the other <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/fliplines-and-lanyards/lanyard-kits/">lanyard kits</a> we carry.',
            2 => 'Choose your lanyard length based on the stems you climb most. A longer lanyard wraps bigger trunks and gives more room to adjust, while a shorter one is lighter and easier to manage on smaller trees. Check the kit\'s listed length before ordering, and remember you can always add a second lanyard later.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Using and inspecting the kit',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Confirm what the kit includes and assemble or adjust it only as Yale\'s instructions allow. A lanyard is life-support gear: it must meet the applicable standard, be used within ANSI Z133 and be used by trained climbers.',
            1 => 'Check the rope, splice, snap gate and adjuster before every climb. A rope lanyard can be cut by a saw in a moment, so keep the bar away from it. Retire it after a cut, heat damage, a shock load or a gate that does not lock fully.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Snap or carabiner on a lanyard?',
          'a' => 'Both work. Snaps sit flat in side D-rings and clip quickly; carabiners are more versatile. Choose what your saddle and training suit.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I add a mechanical adjuster?',
          'a' => 'Only use adjusters the rope and kit are approved for, and set them up as the manufacturers instruct.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
        1 => 'safety',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/yale-cordage/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/lanyard-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/lanyard-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Arborist climbing on the tree',
        'creator' => 'Yuliya Krasylenko',
        'creator_url' => 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Yuliya_Krasylenko',
        'license' => 'CC BY 4.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=97167024',
      ),
    ),
    '/climbing/climbing-gear/fliplines-and-lanyards/lanyard-kits/yale-r-i-n-g-positioning-lanyard-kit/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/fliplines-and-lanyards/lanyard-kits/yale-r-i-n-g-positioning-lanyard-kit/',
      'category' => '/climbing/climbing-gear/fliplines-and-lanyards/lanyard-kits/',
      'name' => 'Yale R.I.N.G. Positioning Lanyard Kit',
      'brand' => 'yale-cordage',
      'brand_name' => 'Yale Cordage',
      'kind' => 'lanyard',
      'price' => 139,
      'keyword' => 'yale ring positioning lanyard kit',
      'title' => 'Yale R.I.N.G. Positioning Lanyard Kit',
      'h1' => 'Yale R.I.N.G. Positioning Lanyard Kit',
      'meta' => 'The Yale R.I.N.G. positioning lanyard kit gives tree climbers an adjustable second attachment for spar and limb work. What is included and how to inspect it.',
      'tagline' => 'An adjustable positioning lanyard kit built on Yale R.I.N.G. rope.',
      'summary' => 'The Yale R.I.N.G. positioning lanyard kit is an adjustable lanyard built on Yale Cordage rope, ready to be your second point of attachment in the tree. Choke it around the stem, set the length and lean back to work two-handed.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Built on Yale R.I.N.G. rope',
        1 => 'Adjustable work-positioning lanyard',
        2 => 'Second point of attachment for saw work',
        3 => 'Kit format saves piecing parts together',
        4 => 'From US rope maker Yale Cordage',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Rope',
          1 => 'Yale R.I.N.G.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Positioning lanyard kit',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Yale Cordage',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'The lanyard\'s job',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'On a removal you live on the lanyard. It holds you in place for every spar cut, lets you shift around the stem and backs you up when you move your climbing line. A good one adjusts smoothly, holds firmly and is comfortable to handle all day.',
            1 => 'This kit gives you the rope and hardware to make that happen without sourcing each part yourself. If you want a snap termination instead, see the triple-locking snap version and our other <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/fliplines-and-lanyards/lanyard-kits/">lanyard kits</a>.',
            2 => 'Lanyard kits are also a good way to set up a second lanyard. Many climbers run a short one for limb work and a longer one for spar work on bigger trees. Check the listed length and adjuster before ordering so the kit fits the way you work.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Safety and inspection',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Check the kit contents and assemble it only as Yale\'s instructions specify. A lanyard is life-support gear and must meet the applicable standard, be used within ANSI Z133 and be used by trained climbers.',
            1 => 'Before every climb, check the rope for cuts, glazing and stiff spots, the splice for slippage, and the connectors for full locking. A rope lanyard can be cut by a saw instantly; on heavy spar work many climbers add a wire-core flipline.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What is the difference from the triple-locking snap kit?',
          'a' => 'The snap kit is terminated with a triple-locking snap. Check this kit\'s listing for its connector setup.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How long should my lanyard be?',
          'a' => 'Long enough to wrap the largest stems you climb with room to adjust. Many climbers own a short and a long one.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'climbing',
        1 => 'safety',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/yale-cordage/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/lanyard-3.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/lanyard-3-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'TVCF004',
        'creator' => 'Symic',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/73344134@N00',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/73344134@N00/33549425170',
      ),
