          'h' => 'Why throw line needs its own storage',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A small throw line bag suits climbers who carry a shorter line, or who want a light bag that fits in a saddle bag or climbing kit. It is just big enough for the line and weight, so it does not take up room you need for other gear.',
            1 => 'Thin throw line tangles faster than anything else in the truck. A loose pile turns into a bird\'s nest the moment you try to throw from it, and untangling it eats time at the start of every job. Keeping the line in a container that opens wide and lets it flake out cleanly is the easiest fix. Compare options in our <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/gear-storage/">gear storage</a> section.',
