      'keyword' => 'weaver wlc-530 climbing saddle',
      'title' => 'Weaver WLC-530 Climbing Saddle',
      'h1' => 'Weaver WLC-530 Climbing Saddle',
      'meta' => 'The Weaver WLC-530 climbing saddle for daily tree work. Who it suits, how it compares to Weaver\'s other saddles, fitting advice, and daily inspection points.',
      'tagline' => 'A Weaver climbing saddle built for everyday tree work.',
      'summary' => 'The Weaver WLC-530 climbing saddle is one of Weaver Leather\'s tree climbing saddles, built for working climbers who want a padded, durable saddle for daily pruning and removals. Check the current Weaver spec sheet for exact sizing and attachment details before you buy.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Weaver tree climbing saddle for daily work',
        1 => 'Padded for comfort in the work position',
        2 => 'Side D-rings for lanyard and flipline',
        3 => 'Durable construction for removal work',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Model',
          1 => 'WLC-530',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Tree climbing saddle',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Maker',
          1 => 'Weaver Leather',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Where the WLC-530 fits',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Weaver\'s WLC saddles cover a range from basic to fully featured. The WLC-530 is aimed at the climber who works aloft most days and wants a padded saddle that holds up to spurs, bark, and grit. Side D-rings take a flipline or lanyard for positioning, and the padding helps when you sit back to make cuts.',
            1 => 'If you are choosing between models, compare attachment points, padding, and adjustability with the other options in our <a href="/climbing/saddles-and-harnesses/weaver-saddles/">Weaver saddles</a> section, and pick the one that suits how you climb.',
            2 => 'Saddle choice is personal. Weight, padding, and where the attachment points sit all change how a saddle feels after six hours aloft. If you can, try the WLC-530 on and hang in it before committing, and think about whether you climb mostly on spurs or mostly pruning on rope.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fit, standards, and inspection',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Fit the saddle using Weaver\'s sizing guidance. It should be snug on the hips with the leg loops adjusted so you hang level. Use only a saddle that meets ANSI Z133 and the manufacturer\'s requirements, and make sure you are trained in the climbing system you plan to use.',
            1 => 'Inspect before every climb: webbing, leather, stitching, buckles, and D-rings. Look for cuts, abrasion, heat damage, corrosion, and cracks. Retire the saddle if anything fails inspection.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I use the WLC-530 for SRS?',
          'a' => 'Check Weaver\'s instructions for the approved attachment points and configurations before setting it up for any climbing system.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What should I check before each climb?',
          'a' => 'Webbing, leather, stitching, buckles, and D-rings. Retire the saddle if you find cuts, cracks, heat damage, or distortion.',
        ),
      ),
