      'keyword' => 'arborwear transpiration t-shirt',
      'title' => 'Arborwear Transpiration T-Shirt, Safety Yellow',
      'h1' => 'Arborwear Transpiration T-Shirt (Safety Yellow)',
      'meta' => 'The Arborwear Transpiration t-shirt in safety yellow is a lightweight work tee for hot days on tree crews. Why it suits climbers, fit notes, and hi-vis caveats.',
      'tagline' => 'A lightweight, bright work tee for hot days in the tree and on the ground.',
      'summary' => 'The Arborwear Transpiration t-shirt is a lightweight work tee built for hot days, here in safety yellow. It is made to handle sweat better than a plain cotton tee, and the bright color helps ground workers and climbers stay visible on the job.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Lightweight tee for hot-weather work',
        1 => 'Handles sweat better than plain cotton',
        2 => 'Safety yellow color for visibility',
        3 => 'Comfortable under a saddle',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Type',
          1 => 'Work t-shirt',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Color',
          1 => 'Safety yellow',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Maker',
          1 => 'Arborwear',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Built for summer tree work',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'July removals are hard enough without a soaked cotton shirt sticking to your back. A tee made to move moisture helps keep you a little cooler and drier through a long climb or a day of feeding the chipper. The bright color helps the climber see the ground crew and the ground crew see each other near equipment and traffic.',
            1 => 'It layers under a work shirt or sweatshirt on cooler mornings too. Browse more crew clothing in our <a href="/clothing/">clothing</a> section.',
            2 => 'Lightweight tees also dry faster when you take a break, which helps when you climb back up after lunch. Many crews buy them in bulk and wear a fresh one each day through the hottest months.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fit and safety notes',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Pick a fit that does not ride up when you reach or lean back in a saddle, and that is not so loose it catches on branches. Keep any loose clothing away from chippers and stump grinders.',
            1 => 'A safety yellow tee adds visibility but is not a substitute for ANSI-rated high-visibility apparel where the job or a road work zone requires it. Drink water, take breaks in the shade, and watch your crew for signs of heat illness on hot days.',
            2 => 'Wash it per the care label.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is this t-shirt rated high-visibility apparel?',
          'a' => 'Treat it as a bright work tee. Use certified high-visibility apparel where a job or work zone requires it.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does it work as a base layer in winter?',
          'a' => 'Yes. It can be worn under a sweatshirt or fleece on cold days.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'apparel',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/arborwear/',
