          1 => 'Pole pruner head',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Connection',
          1 => 'CompositLock',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'What it is for',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A pruner head turns a pole into a clean-cutting tool for limbs you cannot reach from the ground. It is the right choice for smaller limbs where a saw is overkill and a clean cut matters, such as raising a canopy or removing small deadwood.',
            1 => 'The CompositLock fitting must match your poles, so check before you order. Other heads and pruners are in <a href="/cutting-and-pruning/pruners-and-loppers/">pruners and loppers</a>.',
            2 => 'Replacing just the head makes sense when the poles are still in good shape but the old head is worn, bent or missing parts. A fresh head with a sharp blade and smooth pivot cuts more cleanly and takes less effort on the rope, which makes a big difference on a long day of clearance pruning.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Safe use and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Wear a helmet and eye protection and stand to the side of the cut. Keep clear of power lines; do not count on a pole for electrical protection.',
            1 => 'Keep the blade clean and sharp, oil the pivot and pulley, and check the rope and fittings before each job. Replace worn rope and damaged parts promptly.',
            2 => 'Keep the pruner head covered and stored in a pole bag when it is not in use, so the blade stays sharp and nobody grabs it by the cutting end. A spare blade and rope in the bag can save a trip back to the shop.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does this include rope and poles?',
          'a' => 'This listing is the pruner head. Check the product details for included rope, and add poles separately.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will it fit non-Jameson poles?',
          'a' => 'It is designed for the CompositLock connection. Confirm your pole fitting before buying.',
        ),
      ),
