          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Jameson',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Built for steady work',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Pole pruners on a busy crew take a beating: dropped in the truck, banged into limbs, pulled hard on wet days. A heavy duty head stands up to that and keeps cutting cleanly. It is a good fit for clearance pruning, line-of-sight work and canopy raising.',
            1 => 'Match the head to your pole connection and add rope if needed. Compare heads in <a href="/cutting-and-pruning/pruners-and-loppers/">pruners and loppers</a>.',
            2 => 'Pole pruners are the right tool for small limbs that need a clean cut, especially on street trees and ornamentals. They are quiet, need no fuel, and are easy to hand to a ground worker. A heavy duty head gives you that clean cut and holds up to the knocks of daily work.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Use and maintenance',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Seat the limb fully in the jaw before pulling, stand off to the side, and wear a helmet and eye protection. Keep the required clearance from power lines.',
            1 => 'Clean and oil the pivot and pulley, keep the blade sharp, and inspect the rope for wear. Replace worn parts before they fail on the job.',
            2 => 'Keep a spare blade and rope with the kit so a worn part does not stop the job. Store the pruner in a pole bag with the cutting head covered, and keep it out of the bottom of the truck where heavy gear can bend it.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does it come with a rope?',
          'a' => 'Check the listing details. Pruner heads are often sold without poles, and rope may be separate.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can the blade be replaced?',
          'a' => 'Jameson pruner heads are serviceable, and replacement blades are available for common models.',
        ),
