          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna 395XP (confirm your model/serial)',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Air filter felt',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Protect the big saw',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A 395XP is usually the felling and bucking saw for the biggest wood on the job. It works hard and makes a lot of chips. A plugged felt robs it of power and a torn one lets dust wear the piston and rings. Both are cheap to fix compared with a top end.',
            1 => 'Find more 395XP and other parts in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">power equipment parts</a>.',
            2 => 'Big saws also tend to sit in the truck between jobs, which means dust settles into the filter area. Check the felt before starting a saw that has been parked for a while.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Checking and replacing',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Look at the felt every tank on dusty work. Clean it as Husqvarna recommends, and replace it if it is torn, matted with oil, or no longer seals.',
            1 => 'Make sure the felt sits right in the filter housing before you close the cover so air cannot bypass it.',
            2 => 'Carry a spare felt in the saw kit so you can swap a dirty one in the field and clean it later. If you see dust inside the carb side of the filter, the filter isn\'t sealing; find out why before running the saw again. Check the carburetor intake for dust each time you change the filter.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I wash the felt?',
          'a' => 'Follow Husqvarna\'s cleaning instructions for your filter. Replace it if it\'s torn or won\'t come clean.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I know it\'s the right part?',
          'a' => 'Match it to your saw\'s model and serial number in the Husqvarna parts listing.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
