      'keyword' => 'husqvarna 550xp mark ii cylinder gasket',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna 550XP Mark II Cylinder Gasket',
      'h1' => 'Cylinder Gasket for Husqvarna 550XP Mark II',
      'meta' => 'A Husqvarna 550XP Mark II cylinder gasket for top-end rebuilds. Keep a fresh one on hand so the saw seals, holds compression, and doesn\'t run lean.',
      'tagline' => 'A replacement cylinder gasket for the Husqvarna 550XP Mark II.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna 550XP Mark II cylinder gasket is a new seal for when the cylinder comes off for a piston, rings, or a cleanup after a lean seize. The 550XP Mark II is a common ground saw on tree crews, and gaskets are worth keeping in the parts bin.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'For the 550XP Mark II',
        1 => 'New seal for top-end service',
        2 => 'Helps prevent air leaks',
        3 => 'Inexpensive part to stock',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Husqvarna',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna 550XP Mark II (confirm model/serial)',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Cylinder gasket',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'When you need one',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Scored piston, broken ring, or a cylinder pulled to check for damage: each one means a new gasket. The old gasket has already been compressed and will not seal again reliably.',
            1 => 'Order the gasket with any other top-end parts so the saw is not down twice. See our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">power equipment parts</a> for the rest.',
            2 => 'Small parts like this are easy to forget until the saw is in pieces on the bench. If you run several 550XP Mark II saws, keep a few gaskets in the parts drawer so a rebuild doesn\'t stall waiting for shipping.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Getting a good seal',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Clean the surfaces carefully, follow the bolt torque and pattern in the service manual, and pressure and vacuum test the engine if you can.',
            1 => 'An air leak after a rebuild makes the saw run lean and hot. Fix the cause of the original failure, often a dirty filter or an air leak, before running it hard.',
            2 => 'Before the saw goes back to work, check the air filter, fuel filter, and intake boot, and retune the carburetor. A new gasket won\'t save an engine that is still running lean. Confirm the part number for your serial range, as small changes over a production run can affect fit.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is this different from the base gasket?',
          'a' => 'Names vary between sellers. Check the Husqvarna part number for your saw.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Do I need sealant?',
          'a' => 'Follow the service manual. Most cylinder gaskets go in dry.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/parts-1.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/parts-1-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Route Clearance',
