      'title' => 'Husqvarna 395XP Inlet Pipe (Intake Boot)',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Inlet Pipe for 395XP Chainsaw',
      'meta' => 'A replacement Husqvarna 395XP intake boot, also called the inlet pipe, that joins carburetor and cylinder. A cracked boot causes air leaks and lean seizures.',
      'tagline' => 'A replacement inlet pipe, or intake boot, for the Husqvarna 395XP.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna 395XP intake boot, listed as the inlet pipe, connects the carburetor to the cylinder. When the rubber cracks or hardens, the saw pulls in extra air, runs lean, and risks scoring the piston.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Replacement for the 395XP',
        1 => 'Seals carburetor to cylinder',
        2 => 'Prevents lean-running air leaks',
        3 => 'Common wear item on older saws',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Husqvarna',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna 395XP (confirm model/serial)',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Inlet pipe / intake boot',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why intake boots fail',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Heat, age, and fuel break down the rubber over time. A cracked boot is hard to spot from the outside but shows up as a high, hanging idle, erratic running, or a saw that needs the carburetor richened to run. Left alone, it can lead to a lean seizure.',
            1 => 'If the boot is bad, check the impulse line too. Both are in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">power equipment parts</a>.',
            2 => 'Pull the air filter and look at the boot with a light. Cracks often appear on the outside of a bend where you can\'t see them with the carb installed. A boot that feels hard and stiff rather than soft is due for replacement.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting it',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Follow the service manual for removing the carburetor and seating the new boot. It must sit fully on both the carb and the cylinder with no twist.',
            1 => 'A vacuum test after installation confirms the seal. Then retune the carburetor, since an air leak may have hidden a lean setting.',
            2 => 'Match the part number to your 395XP\'s serial range. If you\'re not comfortable working on the intake, have a qualified shop do the job and pressure test the saw. Keep the old boot until the new one is installed and tested, in case there\'s a question about fit.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is the inlet pipe the same as the intake boot?',
          'a' => 'Yes. Husqvarna calls it the inlet pipe; many techs call it the intake boot or manifold.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I test for an air leak?',
          'a' => 'Use a pressure and vacuum tester on the sealed engine.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/parts-3.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/parts-3-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Sharpening Chainsaw Blades',
        'creator' => 'NCDOTcommunications',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/39320593@N03',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/39320593@N03/36914543386',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-seal-for-372xp-x-torque/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-seal-for-372xp-x-torque/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Seal for 372XP X-Torque',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'parts',
      'price' => 10,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna 372xp seal',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna 372XP X-Torque Seal Replacement',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Seal for 372XP X-Torque',
      'meta' => 'A replacement Husqvarna 372XP seal for the X-Torque model. Worn seals let air or oil past and cause lean running and leaks. Check the position first.',
      'tagline' => 'A replacement seal for the Husqvarna 372XP X-Torque.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna 372XP seal is a replacement part for the X-Torque version of the 372XP. Seals keep air, fuel, and oil where they belong, and a worn one can cause lean running or leaks.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'For the 372XP X-Torque',
        1 => 'Replaces a worn or leaking seal',
        2 => 'Helps keep the engine sealed',
        3 => 'Low-cost part for rebuilds',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Husqvarna',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna 372XP X-Torque (confirm model/serial)',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Seal',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Confirm which seal you need',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A saw uses several seals, and the most common ones are crankshaft seals on each side of the engine. Check the Husqvarna parts diagram for your model and serial to be sure this is the seal for the position you are replacing.',
            1 => 'Browse more 372XP parts in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">power equipment parts</a>.',
            2 => 'Seals harden with age and heat. Saws that have run hot, sat for a long time, or had a lean seizure are more likely to need new ones. Replacing them during a rebuild avoids a second teardown.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Signs and install notes',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'A leaking crank seal often shows up as a high or erratic idle that won\'t tune out, or fuel residue around the flywheel or clutch side. A pressure and vacuum test pinpoints it.',
            1 => 'Install seals square, without nicking the lip, and with the right tool. A damaged lip will leak from the start.',
            2 => 'If you don\'t have the tools or a tester, a qualified shop can do the job quickly. A saw that runs lean from a bad seal can damage the piston and cylinder in minutes of hard cutting. Keep spare seals in the parts drawer if you run several 372XP X-Torque saws. Lubricate the seal lip lightly before fitting so it doesn\'t run dry on startup.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Which seal is this?',
          'a' => 'Check the parts diagram for your 372XP X-Torque to match the position before ordering.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can a bad seal ruin my saw?',
          'a' => 'Yes. An air leak makes the saw run lean, which can score the piston and cylinder.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/parts-0.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/parts-0-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'chainsaw',
        'creator' => 'sf-dvs',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/46207792@N00',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/46207792@N00/64064283',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-seal-for-t540xp-top-handle-chainsaw/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-seal-for-t540xp-top-handle-chainsaw/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Seal for T540XP Top Handle Chainsaw',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'parts',
      'price' => 10,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna t540xp seal',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna T540XP Top Handle Saw Seal Replacement',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Seal for T540XP Top Handle Chainsaw',
      'meta' => 'A replacement Husqvarna T540XP seal for the top-handle climbing saw. Keep the engine sealed so it idles and runs right. Match the position before ordering.',
      'tagline' => 'A replacement seal for the Husqvarna T540XP top-handle saw.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna T540XP seal is a replacement part for Husqvarna\'s top-handle climbing saw. A worn seal lets air or oil past, and on a saw you depend on in the tree, a steady idle and clean running matter.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'For the Husqvarna T540XP',
        1 => 'Replaces a worn or leaking seal',
        2 => 'Helps restore a steady idle',
        3 => 'Small part, big difference in reliability',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Husqvarna',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna T540XP (confirm model/serial)',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Seal',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'A reliable climbing saw',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'When you\'re tied in at the top of a tree, a saw that won\'t idle, dies on you, or creeps the chain is more than a nuisance. Seal leaks are one cause of an unstable idle. Confirm which seal your saw needs using the Husqvarna parts diagram for your model and serial.',
            1 => 'Find more top-handle parts in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">power equipment parts</a>.',
            2 => 'Climbing saws also get a lot of start-stop use, which is hard on the engine. Fixing a leak early saves you from a bigger repair later. Check the intake boot and impulse line at the same time.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Installing and testing',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Use the correct tools to remove and seat seals without damaging the lip or the crankshaft. Pressure and vacuum test the engine after the repair.',
            1 => 'Top-handle saws are for trained arborists working in trees. Follow the operator\'s manual and ANSI Z133.',
            2 => 'If your saw idles poorly or creeps the chain, set it aside until it\'s fixed. A properly tuned saw that returns to idle and stops the chain is essential when working at height. If you\'re unsure, have a qualified shop do the repair and run a pressure and vacuum test. Keep a log of repairs on each climbing saw so the crew knows its history.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Why does my T540XP idle high?',
          'a' => 'An air leak through a seal, an intake leak, or the carburetor setting can all cause it. Test before you replace parts.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is this seal also for the T540i XP?',
          'a' => 'No. The T540i XP is the battery version. This part is for the gas T540XP; confirm with the parts list.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
        1 => 'climbing',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/parts-1.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/parts-1-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Route Clearance',
        'creator' => 'Georgia National Guard',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/40994485@N04',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/40994485@N04/33581236171',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-starter-spring-for-starter-pawl/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-starter-spring-for-starter-pawl/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Starter Spring for Starter Pawl',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'parts',
      'price' => 5,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna starter pawl spring',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna Starter Pawl Spring Replacement',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Starter Spring for Starter Pawl',
      'meta' => 'A Husqvarna starter pawl spring that keeps the starter pawls snapping into the flywheel. Fixes a pull cord that spins freely without catching on many models.',
      'tagline' => 'A small spring that returns the starter pawl on Husqvarna saws.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna starter pawl spring holds the starter pawl in position so it catches when you pull the cord and retracts once the engine fires. A broken or weak spring is a common reason a pull cord spins without turning the engine.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Replacement starter pawl spring',
        1 => 'Fixes a starter that won\'t catch',
        2 => 'Small, inexpensive part',
        3 => 'Fits many Husqvarna saws (check your model)',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Husqvarna',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Starter pawl spring',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna saws (confirm by model)',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'When the cord won\'t catch',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'If the starter rope pulls out but the engine doesn\'t turn, the pawls on the flywheel side are not engaging. Often a pawl spring has broken or lost tension, or a pawl is worn. A quick inspection usually shows the problem.',
            1 => 'Check the pawls and the bolt while you\'re there. Find related starter parts in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">power equipment parts</a>.',
            2 => 'A starter that won\'t catch is frustrating in the shop and worse at the top of a tree. A broken pawl spring is a quick, cheap fix that gets the saw starting again without replacing the whole starter.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fit and install',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Confirm this spring matches your saw\'s model using the Husqvarna parts diagram. Disconnect the spark plug lead before working near the flywheel.',
            1 => 'Clean sawdust out of the flywheel area while it\'s open; packed debris can also keep pawls from moving freely.',
            2 => 'While you have the starter off, check the rope for fraying and the recoil spring for tension. Replace a frayed rope before it breaks. Keep a few pawl springs in the parts drawer, since they are small and easy to lose during a repair. Reassemble with the cover screws tightened evenly. Check the pawl pivots for wear too, as a worn pivot lets the pawl wobble and slip.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Will it fit my saw?',
          'a' => 'Many Husqvarna saws share pawl parts, but confirm with the parts diagram for your model.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is this the recoil spring?',
          'a' => 'No. The recoil spring is the large coiled spring in the starter housing. This is the small pawl spring.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'all',
      'brand_path' => '/husqvarna/',
      'photo' => 
      array (
        'src' => '/assets/photos/parts-2.webp',
        'sm' => '/assets/photos/parts-2-sm.webp',
        'title' => 'Skoda Fabia Inlet Manifold',
        'creator' => 'L.C.Nøttaasen',
        'creator_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/35166455@N00',
        'license' => 'CC BY 2.0',
        'license_url' => 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/',
        'source_url' => 'https://www.flickr.com/photos/35166455@N00/4717400798',
      ),
    ),
    '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-washer-for-395xp-front-anti-vibration-mount/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/husqvarna-washer-for-395xp-front-anti-vibration-mount/',
      'category' => '/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/',
      'name' => 'Husqvarna Washer for 395XP Front Anti-Vibration Mount',
      'brand' => 'husqvarna',
      'brand_name' => 'Husqvarna',
      'kind' => 'parts',
      'price' => 4,
      'keyword' => 'husqvarna 395xp anti vibration washer',
      'title' => 'Husqvarna 395XP Front Anti-Vibration Mount Washer',
      'h1' => 'Husqvarna Washer for 395XP Front Anti-Vibration Mount',
      'meta' => 'A replacement Husqvarna 395XP anti vibration washer for the front AV mount. Keeps the spring seated and the handle tight. Swap it when you replace AV springs.',
      'tagline' => 'A replacement washer for the front anti-vibration mount on the Husqvarna 395XP.',
      'summary' => 'This Husqvarna 395XP anti vibration washer is part of the front AV mount that holds the spring between the handle and the engine. A lost or worn washer can let the spring shift and the handle loosen.',
      'highlights' => 
      array (
        0 => 'For the 395XP front AV mount',
        1 => 'Keeps the AV spring seated',
        2 => 'Helps restore a tight, quiet handle',
        3 => 'Replace along with AV springs',
      ),
      'specs' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Brand',
          1 => 'Husqvarna',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Fits',
          1 => 'Husqvarna 395XP (front AV mount; confirm serial)',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          0 => 'Part type',
          1 => 'Washer',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Small part, important job',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'On a heavy saw like the 395XP, the anti-vibration system takes a lot of load. If the washer goes missing during a repair or wears through, the spring can work loose, the handle rattles, and vibration increases.',
            1 => 'It\'s smart to replace washers with the springs. Find springs and other parts in our <a href="/jobsite/power-equipment/parts/">power equipment parts</a>.',
            2 => 'Washers and small hardware are easy to lose during a repair, and a missing one is enough to make the handle loose. Ordering a spare with your springs saves a second trip. The part costs very little, but a handle that shifts in your grip makes precise cuts harder.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fitting it',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Use the parts diagram to confirm the position and the order of the washer, spring, and screw. Tighten fasteners to spec.',
            1 => 'After the repair, check the handle for slop before running the saw, and inspect the other AV mounts at the same time.',
            2 => 'If you run several 395XP saws, keep a small kit of AV springs, washers, and screws in the shop. Check all mounts at each service, especially on saws that run long bars. A loose handle increases vibration and makes the saw harder to control safely. Hand-tighten first, then torque, so the spring seats evenly without twisting between the handle and the engine bracket.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Do I need this washer if I\'m replacing the spring?',
          'a' => 'If the old washer is worn or missing, yes. It keeps the spring seated.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is this for the rear mounts too?',
          'a' => 'This listing is for the front mount. Check the diagram for other positions.',
        ),
      ),
      'use' => 
      array (
        0 => 'maintenance',
      ),
      'level' => 'pro',
