          'h' => 'Inspection and care',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Keep your climbing line in a rope bag, away from chips, bar oil, fuel and long hours of sun. Never cut near it, and never use it to lower wood. A climbing line that has caught a rigging load is a rigging line from then on.',
            1 => 'Life-support gear must meet ANSI Z133 requirements and the manufacturer\'s instructions, be inspected before every climb, and be used only by trained climbers. Retire the rope if you find cuts, glazing, chemical contact, core damage or a section that feels different from the rest. Compare more <a href="/rope/climbing-rope/16-strand-climbing-rope/">16-strand climbing rope</a>.',
