      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'What the adaptors do',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The Zenith is a popular lightweight helmet, but out of the box it is set up for climbing rather than saw work. The adaptors fit to the sides of the shell and give you mounting points for a Kask visor and earmuffs.',
            1 => 'That turns the Zenith into a full saw helmet setup, so you can wear one helmet for climbing, rigging and running the saw.',
            2 => 'Adaptors are small parts that take a lot of knocks, especially when the helmet gets tossed in the truck or bag. Keep a spare set on hand so a broken mount does not mean working without a visor or muffs. When you replace them, check that your visor and muffs are still in good shape too, since worn parts tend to wear out together.',
