    '/climbing/saddles-and-harnesses/european-saddles/' => 
    array (
      'path' => '/climbing/saddles-and-harnesses/european-saddles/',
      'name' => 'European Saddles',
      'h1' => 'European Climbing Saddles',
      'keyword' => 'european climbing saddle',
      'title' => 'European Climbing Saddles: Petzl, DMM, Treemotion',
      'meta' => 'European climbing saddles for arborists: the Petzl Sequoia, DMM Kinisi Max and Treemotion Pro. Lightweight, adjustable harnesses for long canopy days.',
      'kind' => 'saddle',
      'intro' => 'A European climbing saddle trades bulk for adjustability and freedom of movement. The Petzl Sequoia, DMM Kinisi Max and Treemotion Pro are built for long days in the canopy, especially on SRS.',
      'guide' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'What sets them apart',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'European-style saddles typically use lighter materials, a wide range of adjustment at the waist and legs, and bridge setups that let you swap or tune attachment points. Many climbers find they make SRS and canopy movement easier. Try the fit with your work clothes on, check that gear storage suits your tools, replace bridges per the maker\'s schedule, and inspect before every climb.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Comparing popular models',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The Petzl Sequoia has a long history with arborists, with adjustable leg loops and a comfortable sit. The DMM Kinisi Max is built with SRS climbers in mind, with a focus on comfort and adjustability. The Treemotion Pro is known for its supportive design and wide range of customization. Each has its fans, so try one on if you can. Pay attention to bridge length, how attachment points sit, and how the gear loops work with your tools.',
            1 => 'Many European saddles use replaceable bridges and modular parts, which helps them stay in service longer. Buy genuine replacement parts and follow the manufacturer\'s schedule for swapping bridges and other wear items.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Are European saddles good for spur work?',
          'a' => 'They can be, but some climbers prefer a stiffer American saddle for long days on spurs. Fit and personal preference decide it.',
        ),
      ),
      'parent' => '/climbing/saddles-and-harnesses/',
